[{:db/id 17592186092314 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b1ef773a-e0ea-5eef-bbf3-332e3e7efe2a" "question-c3e46311-f49f-5429-9145-049194bfe241" "question-4c96dcfa-0dd7-50ec-b775-86d1b3c50f89"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186092315 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-5295db33-6fb5-59ca-9a76-f6dda26f7e03"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186092316 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-6f97d30d-8f92-59ad-aa37-53ebf51b3b4c" "question-6838f2f1-19a5-5913-bfcd-14e938b0311d"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-b1ef773a-e0ea-5eef-bbf3-332e3e7efe2a" :question/id #uuid "b1ef773a-e0ea-5eef-bbf3-332e3e7efe2a" :question/math-academy-id "q-143628" :question/problem "Mike has a total of $100$ candies divided into three bags. The first bag contains $18$ mint-flavored candies, while the second bag contains $16$ mint-flavored candies. If $55%$ of all of Mike's candies are mint-flavored, what is the probability that a randomly selected candy is a mint-flavored candy from the third bag?" :question/worked-solution "Let $M$ be the event that the selected candy is mint-flavored, and \n\n- let $A$ be the event that the selected candy is from the first bag,\n\n- let $B$ be the event that the selected candy is from the second bag,\n\n- let $C$ be the event that the selected candy is from the third bag.\n\nThen the disjoint union $A⊔B⊔C$ covers the entire sample space.\n\nRecall that the law of total probability states that\n\n$$\nP(M)=P(M\\cap A)+P(M\\cap B)+P(M\\cap C).\n$$\n\nWe wish to find $P(M\\cap C):$\n\n- To calculate $P(M\\cap A),$ we take the number of mint-flavored candies in the first bag $(18)$ and divide by the total number of candies $(100).$ So, we have\n\n$$\nP(M\\cap A)=\\frac{18}{100}.\n$$\n\n- To calculate $P(M\\cap B),$ we take the number of mint-flavored candies in the second bag $(16)$ and divide by the total number of candies$(100).$ So, we have\n\n$$\nP(M\\cap B)=\\frac{16}{100}.\n$$\n\n- Also, we're given that\n\n$$\nP(M)=55%=\\frac{55}{100}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the above information into the law of total probability and solving for $P(M\\cap C),$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(M) & =P(M\\cap A)+P(M\\cap B)+P(M\\cap C) \\\\ \\frac{55}{100} & =\\frac{18}{100}+\\frac{16}{100}+P(M\\cap C) \\\\ P(M\\cap C) & =\\frac{55}{100}-\\frac{18}{100}-\\frac{16}{100} \\\\ P(M\\cap C) & =\\frac{21}{100} \\\\ P(M\\cap C) & =21%\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b160229e-63c8-5bb3-85c1-a2c73ec30a06"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b160229e-63c8-5bb3-85c1-a2c73ec30a06" :answer-field/id #uuid "b160229e-63c8-5bb3-85c1-a2c73ec30a06" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e9dd86a2-28a9-54a1-bd47-96969ce92071" :answer-field/choices ["answer-623f5887-d90a-5fd9-995d-57c77b99a09d" "answer-e9dd86a2-28a9-54a1-bd47-96969ce92071" "answer-1eeceee9-6b7e-5700-a74d-8554e7f70cc3" "answer-b545930d-e0e3-5eee-bcf2-24a05aca55ad" "answer-d0fd87a2-4baf-59fc-a98d-12d7d2b4e955"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-623f5887-d90a-5fd9-995d-57c77b99a09d" :answer/id #uuid "623f5887-d90a-5fd9-995d-57c77b99a09d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e9dd86a2-28a9-54a1-bd47-96969ce92071" :answer/id #uuid "e9dd86a2-28a9-54a1-bd47-96969ce92071" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "21%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1eeceee9-6b7e-5700-a74d-8554e7f70cc3" :answer/id #uuid "1eeceee9-6b7e-5700-a74d-8554e7f70cc3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "22%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b545930d-e0e3-5eee-bcf2-24a05aca55ad" :answer/id #uuid "b545930d-e0e3-5eee-bcf2-24a05aca55ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "23%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d0fd87a2-4baf-59fc-a98d-12d7d2b4e955" :answer/id #uuid "d0fd87a2-4baf-59fc-a98d-12d7d2b4e955" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-c3e46311-f49f-5429-9145-049194bfe241" :question/id #uuid "c3e46311-f49f-5429-9145-049194bfe241" :question/math-academy-id "q-143630" :question/problem "A certain disease is present in $500$ out of $100\\,000$ people in city $A,$ $800$ out of $200\\,000$ people in city $B,$ and $1\\,100$ out of $500\\,000$ people in city $C.$ What is the probability that a randomly selected person from any city has the disease?" :question/worked-solution "Let $D$ be the event that a person has the disease, and\n\n- let $A$ be the event that the person is from city $A,$\n\n- let $B$ be the event that the person is from city $B,$\n\n- let $C$ be the event that the person is from city $C.$\n\nThen the disjoint union $A⊔B⊔C$ covers the entire sample space.\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected person has the disease, we use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\nP(D)=P(D\\cap A)+P(D\\cap B)+P(D\\cap C)\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that there are a total of \n\n$$\n100\\,000+200\\,000+500\\,000=800\\,000\n$$\n\npeople in all three cities.\n\n- To calculate $P(D\\cap A),$ we take the number of people in city $A$ who have the disease $(500)$ and divide by the total number of people in the three cities $(800\\,000).$ So, we have\n\n$$\nP(D\\cap A)=\\frac{500}{800\\,000}.\n$$\n\n- To calculate $P(D\\cap B),$ we take the number of people in city $B$ who have the disease $(800)$ and divide by the total number of people in the three cities $(800\\,000).$ So, we have\n\n$$\nP(D\\cap B)=\\frac{800}{800\\,000}.\n$$\n\n- To calculate $P(D\\cap C),$ we take the number of people in city $C$ who have the disease $(1\\,100)$ and divide by the total number of people in the three cities $(800\\,000).$ So, we have\n\n$$\nP(D\\cap C)=\\frac{1\\,100}{800\\,000}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the above information into the law of total probability, the probability that a randomly selected person from any city has the disease is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(D) & =P(D\\cap A)+P(D\\cap B)+P(D\\cap C) \\\\  & =\\frac{500}{800\\,000}+\\frac{800}{800\\,000}+\\frac{1\\,100}{800\\,000} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\,400}{800\\,000} \\\\  & =\\frac{24}{8\\,000} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{1\\,000}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1ddb04e3-1a47-50bb-8bb5-20ad79469f4c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1ddb04e3-1a47-50bb-8bb5-20ad79469f4c" :answer-field/id #uuid "1ddb04e3-1a47-50bb-8bb5-20ad79469f4c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b33a5833-4704-5b74-8d07-51d290832266" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b33a5833-4704-5b74-8d07-51d290832266" "answer-13f621be-7da4-57ec-be1a-3bb71fd27cb2" "answer-70fa78ce-a5bb-554d-89bf-e9ff2f2c268f" "answer-021e9a8f-b7c8-5617-b841-181c6dabad37" "answer-7c0bd94e-0737-59fd-971d-a9571075b9e8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b33a5833-4704-5b74-8d07-51d290832266" :answer/id #uuid "b33a5833-4704-5b74-8d07-51d290832266" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{1\\,000}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-13f621be-7da4-57ec-be1a-3bb71fd27cb2" :answer/id #uuid "13f621be-7da4-57ec-be1a-3bb71fd27cb2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{1\\,100}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-70fa78ce-a5bb-554d-89bf-e9ff2f2c268f" :answer/id #uuid "70fa78ce-a5bb-554d-89bf-e9ff2f2c268f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{900}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-021e9a8f-b7c8-5617-b841-181c6dabad37" :answer/id #uuid "021e9a8f-b7c8-5617-b841-181c6dabad37" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{1\\,500}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7c0bd94e-0737-59fd-971d-a9571075b9e8" :answer/id #uuid "7c0bd94e-0737-59fd-971d-a9571075b9e8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{800}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-4c96dcfa-0dd7-50ec-b775-86d1b3c50f89" :question/id #uuid "4c96dcfa-0dd7-50ec-b775-86d1b3c50f89" :question/math-academy-id "q-143722" :question/problem "A total of $200$ colored table tennis balls are distributed among three boxes, $A,$ $B,$ and $C.$ Box $A$ contains $20$ green balls, while Box $B$ contains $30$ green balls. If $45%$ of all the balls are green, what is the probability that a randomly selected ball is a green ball from Box $C?$" :question/worked-solution "Let $G$ be the event that the selected ball is green, and\n\n- let $A$ be the event that the selected ball is from box $A$,\n\n- let $B$ be the event that the selected ball is from box $B$,\n\n- let $C$ be the event that the selected ball is from box $C.$\n\nThen the disjoint union $A⊔B⊔C$ covers the entire sample space.\n\nRecall that the law of total probability states that\n\n$$\nP(G)=P(G\\cap A)+P(G\\cap B)+P(G\\cap C).\n$$\n\nWe wish to find $P(G\\cap C):$\n\n- To calculate $P(G\\cap A),$ we take the number of green balls in box $A$ $(20)$ and divide by the total number of balls $(200).$ So, we have \n\n$$\nP(G\\cap A)=\\frac{20}{200}.\n$$\n\n- To calculate $P(G\\cap B),$ we take the number of green balls in box $B$ $(30)$ and divide by the total number of balls $(200).$ So, we have \n\n$$\nP(G\\cap B)=\\frac{30}{200}.\n$$\n\n- Also, we're given that\n\n$$\nP(G)=45%=\\frac{90}{200}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the above information into the law of total probability and solving for $P(G\\cap C),$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(G) & =P(G\\cap A)+P(G\\cap B)+P(G\\cap C) \\\\ \\frac{90}{200} & =\\frac{20}{200}+\\frac{30}{200}+P(G\\cap C) \\\\ P(G\\cap C) & =\\frac{90}{200}-\\frac{20}{200}-\\frac{30}{200} \\\\ P(G\\cap C) & =\\frac{40}{200} \\\\ P(G\\cap C) & =20%\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9aa2967b-23f5-554f-85ed-580439a3657b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9aa2967b-23f5-554f-85ed-580439a3657b" :answer-field/id #uuid "9aa2967b-23f5-554f-85ed-580439a3657b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1a9d603e-b926-5237-8790-115938fc5ec6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-cd730609-69cd-5dce-ba00-d82c5d65d5ac" "answer-1a9d603e-b926-5237-8790-115938fc5ec6" "answer-94008e65-8008-5f2f-98cd-a9a293d66546" "answer-17b422f9-8fe0-59bc-9eec-efa1f37dfae6" "answer-80f55f6c-60e9-5aa3-80c4-2b3c42adb117"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cd730609-69cd-5dce-ba00-d82c5d65d5ac" :answer/id #uuid "cd730609-69cd-5dce-ba00-d82c5d65d5ac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1a9d603e-b926-5237-8790-115938fc5ec6" :answer/id #uuid "1a9d603e-b926-5237-8790-115938fc5ec6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-94008e65-8008-5f2f-98cd-a9a293d66546" :answer/id #uuid "94008e65-8008-5f2f-98cd-a9a293d66546" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-17b422f9-8fe0-59bc-9eec-efa1f37dfae6" :answer/id #uuid "17b422f9-8fe0-59bc-9eec-efa1f37dfae6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "30%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-80f55f6c-60e9-5aa3-80c4-2b3c42adb117" :answer/id #uuid "80f55f6c-60e9-5aa3-80c4-2b3c42adb117" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "35%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186092558 :question/problem "A company manufactures electronic components. Of the components manufactured, $45%$ are produced by the first machine, $25%$ are produced by the second machine, and the third machine produces the remaining.\nIf $8%$ of the components produced by the first machine, $4%$ produced by the second machine, and $5%$ produced by the third machine are defective, what is the probability that a randomly selected component is defective?" :question/worked-solution "Let $D$ be the event that a randomly selected component is defective, and \n\n- let ${B}_{1}$ be the event that the component was produced by the first machine,\n\n- let ${B}_{2}$ be the event that the component was produced by the second machine,\n\n- let ${B}_{3}$ be the event that the component was produced by the third machine.\n\nThen the disjoint union ${B}_{1}⊔{B}_{2}⊔{B}_{3}$ covers the entire sample space.\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected component is defective, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(D) & =P(D\\cap {B}_{1})+P(D\\cap {B}_{2})+P(D\\cap {B}_{3}) \\\\  & =P(D|{B}_{1})P({B}_{1})+P(D|{B}_{2})P({B}_{2})+P(D|{B}_{3})P({B}_{3})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each piece of information into mathematical notation.\n\n- Since the first machine produces $45%$ of the components, the second machine produces $25%$ of the components, the third machine produces the remaining\n\n$$\n100%-(45%+25%)=30%.\n$$\n\nAs a result, we have\n\n$$\nP({B}_{1})=0.45,\\,P({B}_{2})=0.25,\\,P({B}_{3})=0.3.\n$$\n\n- Since $8%$ of the components produced by the first machine, $4%$ produced by the second machine, and $5%$ produced by the third machine are defective, we have\n\n$$\nP(D|{B}_{1})=0.08,\\,P(D|{B}_{2})=0.04,\\,P(D|{B}_{3})=0.05.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability, the probability that a randomly selected component is defective is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(D) & =P(D|{B}_{1})P({B}_{1})+P(D|{B}_{2})P({B}_{2})+P(D|{B}_{3})P({B}_{3}) \\\\  & =(0.08)(0.45)+(0.04)(0.25)+(0.05)(0.3) \\\\  & =0.036+0.01+0.015 \\\\  & =0.061.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186089519 :answer-field/correct 17592186089523 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-5295db33-6fb5-59ca-9a76-f6dda26f7e03" :question/id #uuid "5295db33-6fb5-59ca-9a76-f6dda26f7e03" :question/math-academy-id "q-143752" :question/problem "In a particular park, there are three forests. Forest $A$ occupies $40%$ of the park area, and  $30%$ of its plants are poisonous. Forest $B$ occupies $25%$ of the park area, and $20%$ of its plants are poisonous. Forest $C$ occupies the remaining park area, and $6%$ of its plants are poisonous. What is the probability that a randomly selected plant from this park is poisonous? Assume that the plants are evenly distributed throughout the park." :question/worked-solution "Let $V$ be the event that the plant is poisonous, and \n\n- let $A$ be the event that the plant is from forest $A,$\n\n- let $B$ be the event that the plant is from forest $B,$\n\n- let $C$ be the event that the plant is from forest $C.$\n\nThen the disjoint union $A⊔B⊔C$ covers the entire sample space.\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected plant is poisonous, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(V) & =P(V\\cap A)+P(V\\cap B)+P(V\\cap C) \\\\  & =P(V|A)P(A)+P(V|B)P(B)+P(V|C)P(C)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each piece of information into mathematical notation.\n\n- Since forest $A$ occupies $40%$ of the park area and forest $B$ occupies $25%$, then forest $C$ occupies the remaining\n\n$$\n100%-(40%+25%)=35%.\n$$\n\nAs a result, we have\n\n$$\nP(A)=0.4,\\,P(B)=0.25,\\,P(C)=0.35.\n$$\n\n- Since $30%$ of the plants in forest $A,$ $20%$ of the plants in forest $B$, and $6%$ of the plants in forrest $C$ are poisonous, we have\n\n$$\nP(V|A)=0.3,\\,P(V|B)=0.2,\\,P(V|C)=0.06.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability, the probability that a randomly selected plant in that park is poisonous is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(V) & =P(V|A)P(A)+P(V|B)P(B)+P(V|C)P(C) \\\\  & =(0.3)(0.4)+(0.2)(0.25)+(0.06)(0.35) \\\\  & =0.12+0.05+0.021 \\\\  & =0.191.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ed1fa99e-a491-5eba-bafa-dde6be00551b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ed1fa99e-a491-5eba-bafa-dde6be00551b" :answer-field/id #uuid "ed1fa99e-a491-5eba-bafa-dde6be00551b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-89585630-1207-54f3-a6dd-d0dda6b0d569" :answer-field/choices ["answer-09666b40-5355-57b1-8b42-60c63995a1c6" "answer-1f8ba24e-a713-55d8-8ec1-c3ba12f16e7e" "answer-83b5f13c-3fd2-5d10-b864-2eb89194f1c2" "answer-89585630-1207-54f3-a6dd-d0dda6b0d569" "answer-ce33935e-f5d0-55b5-9281-89fcc88c0258"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-09666b40-5355-57b1-8b42-60c63995a1c6" :answer/id #uuid "09666b40-5355-57b1-8b42-60c63995a1c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.030" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1f8ba24e-a713-55d8-8ec1-c3ba12f16e7e" :answer/id #uuid "1f8ba24e-a713-55d8-8ec1-c3ba12f16e7e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.035" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-83b5f13c-3fd2-5d10-b864-2eb89194f1c2" :answer/id #uuid "83b5f13c-3fd2-5d10-b864-2eb89194f1c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.116" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-89585630-1207-54f3-a6dd-d0dda6b0d569" :answer/id #uuid "89585630-1207-54f3-a6dd-d0dda6b0d569" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.191" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ce33935e-f5d0-55b5-9281-89fcc88c0258" :answer/id #uuid "ce33935e-f5d0-55b5-9281-89fcc88c0258" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.233" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-6f97d30d-8f92-59ad-aa37-53ebf51b3b4c" :question/id #uuid "6f97d30d-8f92-59ad-aa37-53ebf51b3b4c" :question/math-academy-id "q-143945" :question/problem "In a particular national park, there are three forests. Forest $A$ occupies $40%$ of the park's total area, and $30%$ of the plants it contains are poisonous, while forest $B$ occupies $25%$ of the park's total area, and $20%$ of the plants it has are poisonous. Forest $C$ occupies the remaining area of the park. If the probability that a randomly selected plant from the park is poisonous is $0.24,$ what percentage of plants from forest $C$ are poisonous? Assume that the plants are evenly distributed throughout the park." :question/worked-solution "Let $V$ be the event that a randomly selected plant is poisonous, and \n\n- let $A$ be the event that the plant is from forest $A,$\n\n- let $B$ be the event that the plant is from forest $B,$\n\n- let $C$ be the event that the plant is from forest $C.$\n\nThen the disjoint union $A⊔B⊔C$ covers the entire sample space. \n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected plant is poisonous, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(V) & =P(V\\cap A)+P(V\\cap B)+P(V\\cap C) \\\\  & =P(V|A)P(A)+P(V|B)P(B)+P(V|C)P(C)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each piece of information into mathematical notation.  \n\n- Since forest $A$ occupies $40%$ of the total park land and  forest $B$ occupies $25%$, then forest $C$ occupies the remaining\n\n$$\n100%-(40%+25%)=35%.\n$$\n\nAs a result, we have\n\n$$\nP(A)=0.4,\\,P(B)=0.25,\\,P(C)=0.35.\n$$\n\n- Since $30%$ of the plants in forest $A$ and $20%$ of the plants in forest $B$ are poisonous, we have\n\n$$\nP(V|A)=0.3,\\,P(V|B)=0.2\n$$\n\n- Since the probability that a randomly selected plant from the park is poisonous is $0.24,$ we have\n\n$$\nP(V)=0.24.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability and solving for $P(V|C),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(V) & =P(V|A)P(A)+P(V|B)P(B)+P(V|C)P(C) \\\\ 0.24 & =(0.3)(0.4)+(0.2)(0.25)+P(V|C)(0.35) \\\\ 0.24 & =0.12+0.05+0.35P(V|C) \\\\ 0.35P(V|C) & =0.07 \\\\ P(V|C) & =0.2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $20%$ of plants from forest $C$ are poisonous." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-81cebeb7-8aa0-5776-9a06-8fc04eda14d5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-81cebeb7-8aa0-5776-9a06-8fc04eda14d5" :answer-field/id #uuid "81cebeb7-8aa0-5776-9a06-8fc04eda14d5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-53550687-5bc6-5d71-b56f-d4df929d00c1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f673d168-be18-50e2-a30f-7e13848f8d60" "answer-745015e3-e981-5fcb-a0d8-9fc8adee58db" "answer-53550687-5bc6-5d71-b56f-d4df929d00c1" "answer-07a8bb0b-fd79-5284-a3d7-a5bcb76e5c04" "answer-de4f9499-4120-5b2b-9957-fb77ce79db15"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f673d168-be18-50e2-a30f-7e13848f8d60" :answer/id #uuid "f673d168-be18-50e2-a30f-7e13848f8d60" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-745015e3-e981-5fcb-a0d8-9fc8adee58db" :answer/id #uuid "745015e3-e981-5fcb-a0d8-9fc8adee58db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-53550687-5bc6-5d71-b56f-d4df929d00c1" :answer/id #uuid "53550687-5bc6-5d71-b56f-d4df929d00c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-07a8bb0b-fd79-5284-a3d7-a5bcb76e5c04" :answer/id #uuid "07a8bb0b-fd79-5284-a3d7-a5bcb76e5c04" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "22%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-de4f9499-4120-5b2b-9957-fb77ce79db15" :answer/id #uuid "de4f9499-4120-5b2b-9957-fb77ce79db15" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-6838f2f1-19a5-5913-bfcd-14e938b0311d" :question/id #uuid "6838f2f1-19a5-5913-bfcd-14e938b0311d" :question/math-academy-id "q-143902" :question/problem "Three bags, $A,B,$ and $C,$ contain marbles. Bag $A$ contains $12$ red and $8$ green marbles, while bag $B$ contains $14$ red and $6$ green marbles. A bag is selected at random, and a marble is randomly selected from the bag. If the probability that the selected marble is green is $\\frac{2}{5},$  what proportion of marbles from bag $C$ are green?" :question/worked-solution "Let $G$ be the event of selecting a green marble at random from one of the three bags, and \n\n- let $A$ be the event that the marble is from bag $A,$\n\n- let $B$ be the event that the marble is from bag $B,$\n\n- let $C$ be the event that the marble is from bag $C.$\n\nThen the disjoint union $A⊔B⊔C$ covers the entire sample space. \n\nTo calculate the probability of selecting a green marble, we can use the law of total probability: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(G) & =P(G\\cap A)+P(G\\cap B)+P(G\\cap C) \\\\  & =P(G|A)P(A)+P(G|B)P(B)+P(G|C)P(C)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each piece of information into mathematical notation.\n\n- Since a bag is selected at random, we have\n\n$$\nP(A)=P(B)=P(C)=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$\n\n- Since there are $8$ green marbles out of $20$  in bag $A,$ and  $6$ green marbles out of $20$  in bag $B,$ we have \n\n$$\nP(G|A)=\\frac{8}{20},\\,P(G|B)=\\frac{6}{20}.\n$$\n\n- Since the probability of picking a green marble  from one of the bags is $\\frac{2}{5},$ we have\n\n$$\nP(G)=\\frac{2}{5}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability and solving for $P(G|C),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(G) & =P(G|A)P(A)+P(G|B)P(B)+P(G|C)P(C) \\\\ \\frac{2}{5} & =(\\frac{8}{20})(\\frac{1}{3})+(\\frac{6}{20})(\\frac{1}{3})+P(G|C)(\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\ \\frac{2}{5} & =\\frac{2}{15}+\\frac{1}{10}+(\\frac{1}{3})P(G|C) \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot P(G|C) & =\\frac{2}{5}-\\frac{2}{15}-\\frac{1}{10} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot P(G|C) & =\\frac{1}{6} \\\\ P(G|C) & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{1}{2}$ of the marbles from bag $C$ are green." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ffe4c3f0-bc0e-50f0-bcdc-1b3ec7c8a111"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ffe4c3f0-bc0e-50f0-bcdc-1b3ec7c8a111" :answer-field/id #uuid "ffe4c3f0-bc0e-50f0-bcdc-1b3ec7c8a111" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3acf24ec-8a67-54b8-9448-b5fcd88660d7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3acf24ec-8a67-54b8-9448-b5fcd88660d7" "answer-0506ec88-a559-5e5a-a458-6fc52ef5c6ca" "answer-49850079-8fcd-5314-a588-f2594bdc6cde" "answer-53c3616a-163e-56aa-81e3-423c9687314d" "answer-fa17c92e-61ad-528a-bb3c-cafbd0c254a6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3acf24ec-8a67-54b8-9448-b5fcd88660d7" :answer/id #uuid "3acf24ec-8a67-54b8-9448-b5fcd88660d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0506ec88-a559-5e5a-a458-6fc52ef5c6ca" :answer/id #uuid "0506ec88-a559-5e5a-a458-6fc52ef5c6ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-49850079-8fcd-5314-a588-f2594bdc6cde" :answer/id #uuid "49850079-8fcd-5314-a588-f2594bdc6cde" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-53c3616a-163e-56aa-81e3-423c9687314d" :answer/id #uuid "53c3616a-163e-56aa-81e3-423c9687314d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fa17c92e-61ad-528a-bb3c-cafbd0c254a6" :answer/id #uuid "fa17c92e-61ad-528a-bb3c-cafbd0c254a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054670 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-99e2d98d-7a51-5b32-adc6-16bc3dbb4639" "question-7ca39e1b-3be6-5060-ba61-ae9bf319f824"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-99e2d98d-7a51-5b32-adc6-16bc3dbb4639" :question/id #uuid "99e2d98d-7a51-5b32-adc6-16bc3dbb4639" :question/math-academy-id "q-103212" :question/problem "If ${a}_{n+2}={a}_{n+1}+{a}_{n}$ with ${a}_{1}=-1$ and ${a}_{2}=1,$ then ${a}_{4}=$" :question/worked-solution "To compute ${a}_{4},$ we first need to compute ${a}_{3}.$ So, we substitute $n=1$ into the recursive formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n+2} & ={a}_{n+1}+{a}_{n} \\\\ {a}_{1+2} & ={a}_{1+1}+{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{3} & ={a}_{2}+{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{3} & =1+(-1) \\\\ {a}_{3} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, to compute ${a}_{4},$ we substitute $n=2$ into the recursive formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{2+2} & ={a}_{2+1}+{a}_{2} \\\\ {a}_{4} & ={a}_{3}+{a}_{2} \\\\ {a}_{4} & =0+1 \\\\ {a}_{4} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${a}_{4}=1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6d59a4a8-c488-5e3c-8591-ed1508ff985d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6d59a4a8-c488-5e3c-8591-ed1508ff985d" :answer-field/id #uuid "6d59a4a8-c488-5e3c-8591-ed1508ff985d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-61f8c25d-854a-5100-ac32-71bc61d491c3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-afa5ae3b-a83a-51a5-9c96-b3c49d4685e9" "answer-6d11ffbc-8de8-5be4-996f-e24c275de6f1" "answer-61f8c25d-854a-5100-ac32-71bc61d491c3" "answer-d0b4d9da-b6fd-587d-bfb7-fc901f83469f" "answer-4b068704-3180-59a1-b01b-5e7e1c4e6db8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-afa5ae3b-a83a-51a5-9c96-b3c49d4685e9" :answer/id #uuid "afa5ae3b-a83a-51a5-9c96-b3c49d4685e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6d11ffbc-8de8-5be4-996f-e24c275de6f1" :answer/id #uuid "6d11ffbc-8de8-5be4-996f-e24c275de6f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-61f8c25d-854a-5100-ac32-71bc61d491c3" :answer/id #uuid "61f8c25d-854a-5100-ac32-71bc61d491c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d0b4d9da-b6fd-587d-bfb7-fc901f83469f" :answer/id #uuid "d0b4d9da-b6fd-587d-bfb7-fc901f83469f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4b068704-3180-59a1-b01b-5e7e1c4e6db8" :answer/id #uuid "4b068704-3180-59a1-b01b-5e7e1c4e6db8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-7ca39e1b-3be6-5060-ba61-ae9bf319f824" :question/id #uuid "7ca39e1b-3be6-5060-ba61-ae9bf319f824" :question/math-academy-id "q-103220" :question/problem "The recursive formula for the Fibonacci numbers is \n\n$$\n{a}_{n+2}={a}_{n+1}+{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}={a}_{2}=1,\\,n\\ge 1.\n$$\n\nWhat is the eighth number in the sequence?" :question/worked-solution "Substituting $n=1$ into the recursive formula gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1+2} & ={a}_{1+1}+{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{3} & ={a}_{2}+{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{3} & =1+1 \\\\ {a}_{3} & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=2$ into the recursive formula gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{2+2} & ={a}_{2+1}+{a}_{2} \\\\ {a}_{4} & ={a}_{3}+{a}_{2} \\\\ {a}_{4} & =2+1 \\\\ {a}_{4} & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=3$ into the recursive formula gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{3+2} & ={a}_{3+1}+{a}_{3} \\\\ {a}_{5} & ={a}_{4}+{a}_{3} \\\\ {a}_{5} & =3+2 \\\\ {a}_{5} & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=4$ into the recursive formula gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{4+2} & ={a}_{4+1}+{a}_{4} \\\\ {a}_{6} & ={a}_{5}+{a}_{4} \\\\ {a}_{6} & =5+3 \\\\ {a}_{6} & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=5$ into the recursive formula gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{5+2} & ={a}_{5+1}+{a}_{5} \\\\ {a}_{7} & ={a}_{6}+{a}_{5} \\\\ {a}_{7} & =8+5 \\\\ {a}_{7} & =13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=6$ into the recursive formula gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{6+2} & ={a}_{6+1}+{a}_{6} \\\\ {a}_{8} & ={a}_{7}+{a}_{6} \\\\ {a}_{8} & =13+8 \\\\ {a}_{8} & =21\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $21$ is the eighth number in the sequence." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-74483277-d70b-52c9-b96e-d2190f446b89"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-74483277-d70b-52c9-b96e-d2190f446b89" :answer-field/id #uuid "74483277-d70b-52c9-b96e-d2190f446b89" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2fd1a056-23c0-5b19-89c0-76e6eedfb9fa" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2fc8ec28-19c8-5852-81cc-746aa47573fb" "answer-2fd1a056-23c0-5b19-89c0-76e6eedfb9fa" "answer-4d62557c-a761-57e0-a0f9-8fb42f0b2d5a" "answer-57173a82-4d10-53b7-9556-2b3b2634fb28" "answer-b5d9d0f3-272c-5aca-a108-a7631f749ccc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2fc8ec28-19c8-5852-81cc-746aa47573fb" :answer/id #uuid "2fc8ec28-19c8-5852-81cc-746aa47573fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "13" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2fd1a056-23c0-5b19-89c0-76e6eedfb9fa" :answer/id #uuid "2fd1a056-23c0-5b19-89c0-76e6eedfb9fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "21" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4d62557c-a761-57e0-a0f9-8fb42f0b2d5a" :answer/id #uuid "4d62557c-a761-57e0-a0f9-8fb42f0b2d5a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "34" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-57173a82-4d10-53b7-9556-2b3b2634fb28" :answer/id #uuid "57173a82-4d10-53b7-9556-2b3b2634fb28" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "55" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b5d9d0f3-272c-5aca-a108-a7631f749ccc" :answer/id #uuid "b5d9d0f3-272c-5aca-a108-a7631f749ccc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054671 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b81eff41-cfe8-5cbc-b97f-aeed5d4a52b5"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-b81eff41-cfe8-5cbc-b97f-aeed5d4a52b5" :question/id #uuid "b81eff41-cfe8-5cbc-b97f-aeed5d4a52b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-214157" :question/problem "If\n$f(n+2)=f(n+1)+f(n)$\nwith\n$f(1)=7$ and $f(2)=-2,$\nthen $f(8)=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The recursion relation is\n\n$$\nf(n+2)=f(n+1)+f(n).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=1$ into the recursive formula gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1+2) & =f(1+1)+f(1) \\\\ f(3) & =f(2)+f(1) \\\\ f(3) & =(-2)+7 \\\\ f(3) & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=2$ into the recursive formula gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2+2) & =f(2+1)+f(2) \\\\ f(4) & =f(3)+f(2) \\\\ f(4) & =5+(-2) \\\\ f(4) & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, substituting $n=3,4,5,6$ into the recursive formula gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(5) & =f(3+2)=f(3+1)+f(3)=f(4)+f(3)=3+5=8, \\\\ f(6) & =f(4+2)=f(4+1)+f(4)=f(5)+f(4)=8+3=11, \\\\ f(7) & =f(5+2)=f(5+1)+f(5)=f(6)+f(5)=11+8=19, \\\\ f(8) & =f(6+2)=f(6+1)+f(6)=f(7)+f(6)=19+11=30.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $f(8)=30.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-19c46680-9993-5640-98e9-22ab2e77aae6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-19c46680-9993-5640-98e9-22ab2e77aae6" :answer-field/id #uuid "19c46680-9993-5640-98e9-22ab2e77aae6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-48a0c375-e447-584a-adc5-cd97b9bc69fe" :answer-field/choices ["answer-48a0c375-e447-584a-adc5-cd97b9bc69fe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-48a0c375-e447-584a-adc5-cd97b9bc69fe" :answer/id #uuid "48a0c375-e447-584a-adc5-cd97b9bc69fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "30" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-aab98372-699b-5aa2-83a4-b5dd4d59f1b8" :activity/id #uuid "aab98372-699b-5aa2-83a4-b5dd4d59f1b8" :activity/title "Fibonacci Sequences" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186050192 :activity/course 17592186046647 :activity/steps ["step-33ac9da8-9392-51b3-a742-d639b595eeed" "step-1b7d0a07-0416-5e62-89de-1ee300451bad" "step-3e777299-f009-525c-afd1-25d71c265c46"] :activity/first-step "step-33ac9da8-9392-51b3-a742-d639b595eeed" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-33ac9da8-9392-51b3-a742-d639b595eeed" :step/id #uuid "33ac9da8-9392-51b3-a742-d639b595eeed" :step/content "question-99e2d98d-7a51-5b32-adc6-16bc3dbb4639" :step/next "step-1b7d0a07-0416-5e62-89de-1ee300451bad" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-1b7d0a07-0416-5e62-89de-1ee300451bad" :step/id #uuid "1b7d0a07-0416-5e62-89de-1ee300451bad" :step/content "question-7ca39e1b-3be6-5060-ba61-ae9bf319f824" :step/next "step-3e777299-f009-525c-afd1-25d71c265c46" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-3e777299-f009-525c-afd1-25d71c265c46" :step/id #uuid "3e777299-f009-525c-afd1-25d71c265c46" :step/content "question-b81eff41-cfe8-5cbc-b97f-aeed5d4a52b5" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186311088 :answer-field/choices 17592186310159] [:db/retract 17592186311198 :answer-field/choices 17592186310146] [:db/retract 17592186311184 :answer-field/choices 17592186310780] {:db/id 17592186311088 :answer-field/correct 17592186310407 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186311198 :answer-field/correct 17592186310128 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186311184 :answer-field/correct 17592186309537 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166938 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ca58d00f-a386-5b1e-a85b-e37b24ea3447"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-ca58d00f-a386-5b1e-a85b-e37b24ea3447" :question/id #uuid "ca58d00f-a386-5b1e-a85b-e37b24ea3447" :question/math-academy-id "q-337284" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]x(t)+[\\begin{aligned}3t \\\\ t\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the system of differential equations. Using the method of variation of parameters, the general solution of the equation can be written in the form\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-3t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}+\\,\\,\\frac{1}{3}$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$3(t-1)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the general solution of an inhomogeneous system can be written as \n\n$$\nx(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{c}(t)$ is the complementary solution (solution of the corresponding homogeneous system) and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nNotice that we are given that\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-3t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}.\n$$\n\nWe'll look for a particular solution in the form\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=Φ\\,u(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix for the corresponding homogeneous system, $f(t)$ is the forcing column vector and\n\n$$\nu(t)=\\int {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nIn our case,\n\n$$\nΦ=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-3t} & 0 \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}],\\,f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}3t \\\\ t\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSince $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix, it must be invertible. Using the formula for the inverse of a $2\\times 2$ matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Φ}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{{e}^{-3t}\\cdot {e}^{-t}-0}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-t} & 0 \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={e}^{4t}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-t} & 0 \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3t} & 0 \\\\ 0 & {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]. \\\\ {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3t} & 0 \\\\ 0 & {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3t \\\\ t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3t{e}^{3t} \\\\ t{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using our formula for $u(t),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(t) & =\\int {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int [\\begin{aligned}3t{e}^{3t} \\\\ t{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\int 3t{e}^{3t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\int t{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating the components by parts, we get the following:\n\n- For the first component, let $u=3t$ and $\\text{d}v={e}^{3t}\\,\\text{d}t.$ Then, $\\text{d}u=3\\,\\text{d}t$ and $v=\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3t}.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 3t{e}^{3t}\\,\\text{d}t & =(3t)\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3t}-\\int \\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3t}(3\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =t{e}^{3t}-\\int {e}^{3t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =t{e}^{3t}-\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3t}(3t-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the second component, let $u=t$ and $\\text{d}v={e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t.$ Then, $\\text{d}u=1\\,\\text{d}t$ and $v={e}^{t}.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int t{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t & =t\\cdot {e}^{t}-\\int {e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =t{e}^{t}-{e}^{t} \\\\  & ={e}^{t}(t-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{p}(t) & =Φ\\,u(t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-3t} & 0 \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3t}(3t-1) \\\\ {e}^{t}(t-1)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}3t-1 \\\\ 3(t-1)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d5413a60-3a3a-5440-92ee-5f361e71fff8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d5413a60-3a3a-5440-92ee-5f361e71fff8" :answer-field/id #uuid "d5413a60-3a3a-5440-92ee-5f361e71fff8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-33978283-6287-570d-93ab-bb7631c431be" :answer-field/choices ["answer-33978283-6287-570d-93ab-bb7631c431be"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-33978283-6287-570d-93ab-bb7631c431be" :answer/id #uuid "33978283-6287-570d-93ab-bb7631c431be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3t-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-14db1be8-51e1-5036-b934-216c3bf6e275" :activity/id #uuid "14db1be8-51e1-5036-b934-216c3bf6e275" :activity/title "Solving Systems of ODEs Using Variation of Parameters" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186050355 :activity/course 17592186046644 :activity/steps ["step-082a26b1-f3c0-5b74-a962-43a65356bce3" "step-1464fa05-0d62-5c01-b491-e56ce5c8e2e8" "step-c1f84e26-b520-572d-b1af-861828868756" "step-0418a620-c5b3-5d53-82c0-63ca1c0bfbbe" "step-4f772438-7511-5d11-8498-5f7b2fa9adee"] :activity/first-step "step-082a26b1-f3c0-5b74-a962-43a65356bce3" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-082a26b1-f3c0-5b74-a962-43a65356bce3" :step/id #uuid "082a26b1-f3c0-5b74-a962-43a65356bce3" :step/content 17592186311737 :step/next "step-1464fa05-0d62-5c01-b491-e56ce5c8e2e8" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-1464fa05-0d62-5c01-b491-e56ce5c8e2e8" :step/id #uuid "1464fa05-0d62-5c01-b491-e56ce5c8e2e8" :step/content 17592186311738 :step/next "step-c1f84e26-b520-572d-b1af-861828868756" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-c1f84e26-b520-572d-b1af-861828868756" :step/id #uuid "c1f84e26-b520-572d-b1af-861828868756" :step/content 17592186311828 :step/next "step-0418a620-c5b3-5d53-82c0-63ca1c0bfbbe" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-0418a620-c5b3-5d53-82c0-63ca1c0bfbbe" :step/id #uuid "0418a620-c5b3-5d53-82c0-63ca1c0bfbbe" :step/content "question-ca58d00f-a386-5b1e-a85b-e37b24ea3447" :step/next "step-4f772438-7511-5d11-8498-5f7b2fa9adee" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-4f772438-7511-5d11-8498-5f7b2fa9adee" :step/id #uuid "4f772438-7511-5d11-8498-5f7b2fa9adee" :step/content 17592186311832 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054757 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-cddb4fef-3bf0-5fcd-a32e-3e190b63414d" "question-5375fdcb-d638-5538-9726-96e9ceb723db"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054500 :question/problem "Rationalize the denominator of $\\dfrac {2}{\\sqrt{3} - 1}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that the denominator's conjugate is $\\sqrt{3} + 1.$\n\nNow, to rationalize the denominator, we multiply both the numerator and denominator by the conjugate $\\sqrt{3} + 1,$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\dfrac {2}{\\sqrt{3} - 1} &= \\[5pt]\n\t\t\\dfrac {2}{\\sqrt{3} - 1} \\cdot \\dfrac {\\sqrt{3} + 1} {\\sqrt{3} + 1} &= \\[5pt]\n\t\t\\dfrac {2\\left(\\sqrt 3 + 1\\right)} {\\left(\\sqrt{3}\\right)^2 - 1^2} &= \\[5pt]\t\n\t\t\\dfrac {2\\left(\\sqrt 3 + 1\\right)} {3 - 1} &= \\[5pt]\t\t\n\t\t\\dfrac {2\\left(\\sqrt 3 + 1\\right)} {2} &= \\[5pt]\t\n\t\t\\sqrt 3 + 1 &\n\t}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054758 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-c3a11ea2-d750-5074-97b6-8095f58d666c" "question-ccc6d1c6-42f6-5241-a388-199d166a1d9f"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054501 :question/problem "Rationalize the denominator of $\\dfrac{6}{\\sqrt{10} - \\sqrt{6}}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that the denominator's conjugate is $\\sqrt{10} + \\sqrt{6}.$\n\nNow, to rationalize the denominator, we multiply both the numerator and denominator by the conjugate $\\sqrt{10} + \\sqrt{6},$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{10}-\\sqrt{6}} & = \\\\ \\frac{6}{\\sqrt{10}-\\sqrt{6}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{10}+\\sqrt{6}}{\\sqrt{10}+\\sqrt{6}} & = \\\\ \\frac{6(\\sqrt{10}+\\sqrt{6})}{(\\sqrt{10})^{2}-(\\sqrt{6})^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{6(\\sqrt{10}+\\sqrt{6})}{10-6} & = \\\\ \\frac{6(\\sqrt{10}+\\sqrt{6})}{4} & = \\\\ \\frac{3(\\sqrt{10}+\\sqrt{6})}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054759 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-082850c1-2de3-5d40-b02c-e3313d031987" "question-4303b0e2-8da8-5cbc-9699-e12d9f977852" "question-5aa76a5d-2fdf-5390-a4d4-41bc22f928df"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054502 :question/problem "Rationalize the denominator of $\\dfrac{2 - \\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{2} + 1}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that the denominator's conjugate is $\\sqrt{2} - 1.$\n\nNow, to rationalize the denominator, we multiply both the numerator and denominator by the conjugate $\\sqrt{2} - 1,$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{2}+1} & = \\\\ \\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{2}+1}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}-1}{\\sqrt{2}-1} & = \\\\ \\frac{(2-\\sqrt{2})(\\sqrt{2}-1)}{(\\sqrt{2}+1)(\\sqrt{2}-1)} & = \\\\ \\frac{2\\sqrt{2}-2-(\\sqrt{2})^{2}+\\sqrt{2}}{(\\sqrt{2})^{2}-(1)^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{2\\sqrt{2}-2-2+\\sqrt{2}}{2-1} & = \\\\ \\frac{2\\sqrt{2}-4+\\sqrt{2}}{1} & = \\\\ 3\\sqrt{2}-4\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-cddb4fef-3bf0-5fcd-a32e-3e190b63414d" :question/id #uuid "cddb4fef-3bf0-5fcd-a32e-3e190b63414d" :question/math-academy-id "q-4401" :question/problem "Rationalize the denominator of $\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{6}-3}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that the denominator's conjugate is $\\sqrt{6}+3.$\n\nNow, to rationalize the denominator, we multiply both the numerator and denominator by the conjugate $\\sqrt{6}+3,$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{6}-3} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{6}-3}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{6}+3}{\\sqrt{6}+3} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}(\\sqrt{6}+3)}{(\\sqrt{6})^{2}-(3)^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{18}+3\\sqrt{3}}{6-9} & = \\\\ \\frac{3\\sqrt{2}+3\\sqrt{3}}{-3} & = \\\\ -\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-acb99c51-6896-524d-b8b0-7a613543b444"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-acb99c51-6896-524d-b8b0-7a613543b444" :answer-field/id #uuid "acb99c51-6896-524d-b8b0-7a613543b444" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a84bd018-6ae4-5681-b5c1-31639af975e2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9dd75a1d-99ae-521b-93f4-5cfc289a669e" "answer-a84bd018-6ae4-5681-b5c1-31639af975e2" "answer-39980635-05c0-5c62-8eb9-387988b28986" "answer-df2b8993-331d-5e31-8c29-2f90541a0f80" "answer-89ad1ecf-b85b-5