:db/id "step-fe99fc10-51d6-55ce-8bf8-4a3e58f9b8d2" :step/id #uuid "fe99fc10-51d6-55ce-8bf8-4a3e58f9b8d2" :step/content 17592186385370 :step/next "step-bac60d39-22a6-5ac6-a280-51042791f62d" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-bac60d39-22a6-5ac6-a280-51042791f62d" :step/id #uuid "bac60d39-22a6-5ac6-a280-51042791f62d" :step/content 17592186167325 :step/next "step-03f2df0e-7127-5bf6-a3cb-55f1736639ac" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-03f2df0e-7127-5bf6-a3cb-55f1736639ac" :step/id #uuid "03f2df0e-7127-5bf6-a3cb-55f1736639ac" :step/content 17592186360484 :step/next "step-3c096bca-7b75-5ffa-8b01-bdd0cb2ca5b9" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-3c096bca-7b75-5ffa-8b01-bdd0cb2ca5b9" :step/id #uuid "3c096bca-7b75-5ffa-8b01-bdd0cb2ca5b9" :step/content 17592186479104 :step/next "step-a1ec6cd0-639d-5c32-a34b-e1f726d9e5e0" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-a1ec6cd0-639d-5c32-a34b-e1f726d9e5e0" :step/id #uuid "a1ec6cd0-639d-5c32-a34b-e1f726d9e5e0" :step/content 17592186383614 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186231170 :answer-field/choices 17592186231171] [:db/retract 17592186231170 :answer-field/choices 17592186231172] [:db/retract 17592186231170 :answer-field/choices 17592186231173] [:db/retract 17592186231170 :answer-field/choices 17592186231174] [:db/retract 17592186231170 :answer-field/choices 17592186231175] {:db/id 17592186231464 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e9fe6faf-8364-54c6-b5c6-ec03e2fb9a2a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-e9fe6faf-8364-54c6-b5c6-ec03e2fb9a2a" :question/id #uuid "e9fe6faf-8364-54c6-b5c6-ec03e2fb9a2a" :question/math-academy-id "q-60624" :question/problem "![](images/43/435f50f68f1d5d206a935ec9b00dcd53e7a68647875e21f36d70379e3915a4c5.png)\n\nFind the area of the triangle." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the height and base of the triangle:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{base} & =12 \\\\ \\text{height} & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle can be found by the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}=\\frac{1}{2}\\times \\text{base}\\times \\text{height}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the values of the base and height, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\times 12\\times 12 \\\\  & =6\\times 12 \\\\  & =72.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's find the units. Since base and height are measured in inches, the area is measured in square inches. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}=72\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-765d86ee-70ad-5e5c-a6c0-9172acef54c7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-765d86ee-70ad-5e5c-a6c0-9172acef54c7" :answer-field/id #uuid "765d86ee-70ad-5e5c-a6c0-9172acef54c7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5fa01b50-fa86-5d42-9d9e-f20c208a1076" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8ec4b3e2-e623-5ec4-96cf-21891cfd3080" "answer-c88701b7-a7fa-56ab-8c32-e6f1ba45d2a8" "answer-99fdabb5-1a73-59b9-810d-855b3e1bb6d4" "answer-5fa01b50-fa86-5d42-9d9e-f20c208a1076" "answer-f083bac5-dd38-5485-a153-68c65a64f5f0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8ec4b3e2-e623-5ec4-96cf-21891cfd3080" :answer/id #uuid "8ec4b3e2-e623-5ec4-96cf-21891cfd3080" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "126\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c88701b7-a7fa-56ab-8c32-e6f1ba45d2a8" :answer/id #uuid "c88701b7-a7fa-56ab-8c32-e6f1ba45d2a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "144\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-99fdabb5-1a73-59b9-810d-855b3e1bb6d4" :answer/id #uuid "99fdabb5-1a73-59b9-810d-855b3e1bb6d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "63\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5fa01b50-fa86-5d42-9d9e-f20c208a1076" :answer/id #uuid "5fa01b50-fa86-5d42-9d9e-f20c208a1076" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "72\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f083bac5-dd38-5485-a153-68c65a64f5f0" :answer/id #uuid "f083bac5-dd38-5485-a153-68c65a64f5f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "98\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186231465 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ecf8daef-9b17-549e-9c51-518ec81d55ec"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186231768 :question/worked-solution "Let's sketch our cake based on the description.\n\n![](images/20/205df21c66b54b84f9b0608baebf49277720738e1fac14219a7631848ea5c19a.png)\n\nThe height and base of the triangle are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{base} & =5, \\\\ \\text{height} & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle can be found by the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}=\\frac{1}{2}\\times \\text{base}\\times \\text{height}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the values of the base and height, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\times 5\\times 3 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\times 15 \\\\  & =7.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's find the units. Since base and height are measured in centimeters, the area is measured in square centimeters. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}=7.5\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186231170 :answer-field/correct "answer-2e40f59c-5c43-5ce3-9fec-419a42be11b6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6ad3516e-b294-5e7c-a474-d9e0c1c6b4cf" "answer-a371e2e3-b68a-5d88-b845-9048a4af13b4" "answer-f445b4ca-4a23-598d-8e00-2f709f5f07d9" "answer-2e40f59c-5c43-5ce3-9fec-419a42be11b6" "answer-f399ef28-c29c-5938-afa7-1520d202501d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6ad3516e-b294-5e7c-a474-d9e0c1c6b4cf" :answer/id #uuid "6ad3516e-b294-5e7c-a474-d9e0c1c6b4cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12.5\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a371e2e3-b68a-5d88-b845-9048a4af13b4" :answer/id #uuid "a371e2e3-b68a-5d88-b845-9048a4af13b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f445b4ca-4a23-598d-8e00-2f709f5f07d9" :answer/id #uuid "f445b4ca-4a23-598d-8e00-2f709f5f07d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2e40f59c-5c43-5ce3-9fec-419a42be11b6" :answer/id #uuid "2e40f59c-5c43-5ce3-9fec-419a42be11b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7.5\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f399ef28-c29c-5938-afa7-1520d202501d" :answer/id #uuid "f399ef28-c29c-5938-afa7-1520d202501d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9.5\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-ecf8daef-9b17-549e-9c51-518ec81d55ec" :question/id #uuid "ecf8daef-9b17-549e-9c51-518ec81d55ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-93149" :question/problem "Claire has sectioned off a triangular area of her garden whose base is $7$ feet and height is $5$ feet to plant some flowers. What is the area of the flowerbed?" :question/worked-solution "Let's sketch the flowerbed based on the description.\n\n![](images/b4/b409d299208280d3be7e33be8e74c3d894fa9f3ad7e5605e4b551b6b0434302a.png)\n\nThe height and base of the triangle are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{base} & =7, \\\\ \\text{height} & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle can be found by the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}=\\frac{1}{2}\\times \\text{base}\\times \\text{height}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the values of the base and height, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\times 7\\times 5 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\times 35 \\\\  & =17.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's find the units. Since base and height are measured in feet, the area is measured in square feet. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}=17.5\\,{\\text{ft}}^{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5a740dc6-0953-53ea-b78c-39bc996dc617"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5a740dc6-0953-53ea-b78c-39bc996dc617" :answer-field/id #uuid "5a740dc6-0953-53ea-b78c-39bc996dc617" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c16fb5a3-adb1-598c-a1b6-a5eb383b33bb" :answer-field/choices ["answer-04136959-5e41-5216-9279-1057512c0bff" "answer-c16fb5a3-adb1-598c-a1b6-a5eb383b33bb" "answer-43cbd2ae-0ecf-5595-a730-c4685cb767c2" "answer-68c29f71-725a-5607-b616-c53b49800b36" "answer-5034e216-50cc-5f90-9470-0f87b0b6f66d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-04136959-5e41-5216-9279-1057512c0bff" :answer/id #uuid "04136959-5e41-5216-9279-1057512c0bff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12\\,{\\text{ft}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c16fb5a3-adb1-598c-a1b6-a5eb383b33bb" :answer/id #uuid "c16fb5a3-adb1-598c-a1b6-a5eb383b33bb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "17.5\\,{\\text{ft}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-43cbd2ae-0ecf-5595-a730-c4685cb767c2" :answer/id #uuid "43cbd2ae-0ecf-5595-a730-c4685cb767c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "22.5\\,{\\text{ft}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-68c29f71-725a-5607-b616-c53b49800b36" :answer/id #uuid "68c29f71-725a-5607-b616-c53b49800b36" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24\\,{\\text{ft}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5034e216-50cc-5f90-9470-0f87b0b6f66d" :answer/id #uuid "5034e216-50cc-5f90-9470-0f87b0b6f66d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "35\\,{\\text{ft}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-171482d0-9733-5990-af68-52e897a70b2e" :activity/id #uuid "171482d0-9733-5990-af68-52e897a70b2e" :activity/title "Areas of Triangles" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048846 :activity/course 17592186046647 :activity/steps ["step-417d8d63-6e21-5e67-9747-6630e9445dd3" "step-b8dfeb6a-a542-5081-9a28-e226e6553d95" "step-8acdd2d7-5504-5f14-bf0e-df9ca76ee416"] :activity/first-step "step-417d8d63-6e21-5e67-9747-6630e9445dd3" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-417d8d63-6e21-5e67-9747-6630e9445dd3" :step/id #uuid "417d8d63-6e21-5e67-9747-6630e9445dd3" :step/content "question-e9fe6faf-8364-54c6-b5c6-ec03e2fb9a2a" :step/next "step-b8dfeb6a-a542-5081-9a28-e226e6553d95" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-b8dfeb6a-a542-5081-9a28-e226e6553d95" :step/id #uuid "b8dfeb6a-a542-5081-9a28-e226e6553d95" :step/content 17592186231768 :step/next "step-8acdd2d7-5504-5f14-bf0e-df9ca76ee416" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-8acdd2d7-5504-5f14-bf0e-df9ca76ee416" :step/id #uuid "8acdd2d7-5504-5f14-bf0e-df9ca76ee416" :step/content "question-ecf8daef-9b17-549e-9c51-518ec81d55ec" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186059823 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-43b89dfd-2b90-59a8-92b5-edcb02011dcc" "question-6b59066d-5e7f-5521-a647-a4e84084b17c"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-43b89dfd-2b90-59a8-92b5-edcb02011dcc" :question/id #uuid "43b89dfd-2b90-59a8-92b5-edcb02011dcc" :question/math-academy-id "q-142493" :question/problem "![](images/28/28f56656e191e342a4815ba74bdd29cba5247fba7d8ab0feca8ffbe0b785ab8c.png)\n\nConsider a sample of size $n=120$  from a population with standard deviation $\\sigma =10.$ Given that the mean of the sample is $\\overset{―}{x}=3,$ find a $95%$ confidence interval for the population mean $\\mu $ of the distribution.\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that $P(Z>1.96)=0.025,$ where $Z∼N(0,1),$ as shown in the diagram above.*" :question/worked-solution "We do not know the distribution of the population. However, the sample size $n=120\\ge 30$ is *sufficiently large*. Therefore, according to the central limit theorem, we may use the following approximation:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\overset{―}{X}-\\mu }{\\sigma /\\sqrt{n}}∼N(0,1),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n- $\\overset{―}{X}$ is the sample mean,\n\n- $\\mu $ is the population mean,\n\n- ${\\sigma }^{2}$ is the population variance, and\n\n- $n$ is the sample size.\n\nGiven a value $\\alpha $ between $0$ and $1,$ the corresponding $[100(1-\\alpha )]%$ confidence interval for the population mean $\\mu $ of the original distribution is given by\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}\\pm {z}_{\\alpha /2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sigma }{\\sqrt{n}},\n$$\n\nwhere $P(Z>{z}_{\\alpha /2})=\\frac{\\alpha }{2}$ and $Z∼N(0,1).$\n\nWe are interested in finding a $95%$ confidence interval. So, we have \n\n$$\n\\alpha =1-0.95=0.05\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\alpha }{2}=0.025.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $P(Z>1.96)=0.025.$ As a result, \n\n$$\n{z}_{\\alpha /2}={z}_{0.025}=1.96.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $95%$ confidence interval for the population mean $\\mu $ is the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\pm 1.96\\cdot \\frac{10}{\\sqrt{120}} \\\\ 3\\pm 1.789\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6dbcdaec-a6e9-53b1-a803-289a0389e11e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6dbcdaec-a6e9-53b1-a803-289a0389e11e" :answer-field/id #uuid "6dbcdaec-a6e9-53b1-a803-289a0389e11e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-78caee98-945d-5e7f-a934-5470d31cd7b8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d86d8d33-0f3d-5bb4-b955-814daea9d8bb" "answer-8d62915a-6993-5f3c-8131-308af074dc45" "answer-c227e7cd-a039-5cfe-a0b7-7ab3d1a522da" "answer-78caee98-945d-5e7f-a934-5470d31cd7b8" "answer-e09fe4af-a846-5ff7-a33c-6662acd0522b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d86d8d33-0f3d-5bb4-b955-814daea9d8bb" :answer/id #uuid "d86d8d33-0f3d-5bb4-b955-814daea9d8bb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "30\\pm 1.63" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8d62915a-6993-5f3c-8131-308af074dc45" :answer/id #uuid "8d62915a-6993-5f3c-8131-308af074dc45" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "30\\pm 17.89" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c227e7cd-a039-5cfe-a0b7-7ab3d1a522da" :answer/id #uuid "c227e7cd-a039-5cfe-a0b7-7ab3d1a522da" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\pm 0.163" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-78caee98-945d-5e7f-a934-5470d31cd7b8" :answer/id #uuid "78caee98-945d-5e7f-a934-5470d31cd7b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\pm 1.789" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e09fe4af-a846-5ff7-a33c-6662acd0522b" :answer/id #uuid "e09fe4af-a846-5ff7-a33c-6662acd0522b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\pm 2.147" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-6b59066d-5e7f-5521-a647-a4e84084b17c" :question/id #uuid "6b59066d-5e7f-5521-a647-a4e84084b17c" :question/math-academy-id "q-142501" :question/problem "![](images/64/6486d3914bb0f7b4898220512e96630d13d2b0f4a5c1851938f98371a4c0255f.png)\n\nConsider a sample of size $n=441$  from a population with standard deviation $\\sigma =5.$ Given that the mean of the sample is $\\overset{―}{x}=15,$ find a $99%$ confidence interval for the population mean $\\mu $ of the distribution.\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that $P(Z>2.576)=0.005,$ where $Z∼N(0,1),$ as shown in the diagram above.*" :question/worked-solution "We do not know the distribution of the population. However, the sample size $n=441\\ge 30$ is *sufficiently large*. Therefore, according to the central limit theorem, we may use the following approximation:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\overset{―}{X}-\\mu }{\\sigma /\\sqrt{n}}∼N(0,1),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n- $\\overset{―}{X}$ is the sample mean,\n\n- $\\mu $ is the population mean,\n\n- ${\\sigma }^{2}$ is the population variance, and\n\n- $n$ is the sample size.\n\nGiven a value $\\alpha $ between $0$ and $1,$ the corresponding $[100(1-\\alpha )]%$ confidence interval for the population mean $\\mu $ of the original distribution is given by\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}\\pm {z}_{\\alpha /2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sigma }{\\sqrt{n}},\n$$\n\nwhere $P(Z>{z}_{\\alpha /2})=\\frac{\\alpha }{2}$ and $Z∼N(0,1).$\n\nWe are interested in finding a $99%$ confidence interval. So, we have \n\n$$\n\\alpha =1-0.99=0.01\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\alpha }{2}=0.005.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $P(Z>2.576)=0.005.$ As a result, \n\n$$\n{z}_{\\alpha /2}={z}_{0.005}=2.576.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $99%$ confidence interval for the population mean $\\mu $ is the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}15\\pm 2.576\\cdot \\frac{5}{\\sqrt{441}} \\\\ 15\\pm 0.613\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-98011249-1f09-5130-9995-976b127cee45"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-98011249-1f09-5130-9995-976b127cee45" :answer-field/id #uuid "98011249-1f09-5130-9995-976b127cee45" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-048e8029-e1b8-52ce-8602-7486fc619b19" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ac69555a-f0da-56b6-9562-d1ad9ad8e1c2" "answer-048e8029-e1b8-52ce-8602-7486fc619b19" "answer-61f12fc8-a6d1-5e75-a753-367524f667c5" "answer-81a28791-38a7-5d17-94a6-fe643ebd793c" "answer-50c3cde0-14e2-5736-8123-072b1aace677"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ac69555a-f0da-56b6-9562-d1ad9ad8e1c2" :answer/id #uuid "ac69555a-f0da-56b6-9562-d1ad9ad8e1c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15\\pm 0.146" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-048e8029-e1b8-52ce-8602-7486fc619b19" :answer/id #uuid "048e8029-e1b8-52ce-8602-7486fc619b19" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15\\pm 0.613" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-61f12fc8-a6d1-5e75-a753-367524f667c5" :answer/id #uuid "61f12fc8-a6d1-5e75-a753-367524f667c5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15\\pm 2.576" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-81a28791-38a7-5d17-94a6-fe643ebd793c" :answer/id #uuid "81a28791-38a7-5d17-94a6-fe643ebd793c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "21\\pm 2.576" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-50c3cde0-14e2-5736-8123-072b1aace677" :answer/id #uuid "50c3cde0-14e2-5736-8123-072b1aace677" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\pm 1.314" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186059824 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-d4daf7f4-d328-5530-aaf2-46c1276ac650"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-d4daf7f4-d328-5530-aaf2-46c1276ac650" :question/id #uuid "d4daf7f4-d328-5530-aaf2-46c1276ac650" :question/math-academy-id "q-142990" :question/problem "A new weight-loss drug is being tested on a sample of $35$ patients. The monthly weight loss of a patient is normally distributed with standard deviation $\\sigma =13\\,\\text{lb}.$ During a particular month, the mean weight loss in the sample is $17.7\\,\\text{lb}.$ Find a $95%$ confidence interval for the mean monthly weight loss $\\mu $ of the entire population.\n\n*Hint: Given a random variable $Z∼N(0,1),$ the table below shows the $z$-scores ${z}_{p}$ such that $P(Z>{z}_{p})=p$ for some particular values of $p.$*\n\n| $p$ | $0.100$ | $0.050$ | $0.025$ | $0.010$ | $0.005$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${z}_{p}$ | $1.282$ | $1.645$ | $1.960$ | $2.326$ | $2.576$ |" :question/worked-solution "We are told that the population is normally distributed. Therefore, the distribution of sample mean is also normal, and we have that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\overset{―}{X}-\\mu }{\\sigma /\\sqrt{n}}∼N(0,1),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n- $\\overset{―}{X}$ is the sample mean,\n\n- $\\mu $ is the population mean,\n\n- ${\\sigma }^{2}$ is the population variance, and\n\n- $n$ is the sample size.\n\nGiven a value $\\alpha $ between $0$ and $1,$ the corresponding $[100(1-\\alpha )]%$ confidence interval for the population mean $\\mu $ of the original distribution is given by\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}\\pm {z}_{\\alpha /2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sigma }{\\sqrt{n}},\n$$\n\nwhere $P(Z>{z}_{\\alpha /2})=\\frac{\\alpha }{2}$ and $Z∼N(0,1).$\n\nIn our case,\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=17.7\\,\\text{lb},\\,n=35,\\,\\sigma =13\\,\\text{lb}.\n$$\n\nWe are interested in finding a $95%$ confidence interval. So, we have \n\n$$\n\\alpha =1-0.95=0.05\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\alpha }{2}=0.025.\n$$\n\nWe also need to find the $z$-score value ${z}_{0.025}$ such that $P(Z>{z}_{0.025})=0.025,$ where $Z∼N(0,1).$\n\n![](images/35/35037db1532092651e1974ea689b6004aa673c29720ac1d1c9d191c5929e9314.png)\n\nFrom the percentage points table of the normal distribution, we obtain that ${z}_{0.025}=1.96:$ \n\n| $p$ | $0.100$ | $0.050$ | $0.025$ | $0.010$ | $0.005$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${z}_{p}$ | $1.282$ | $1.645$ | $1.960$ | $2.326$ | $2.576$ |\n\nTherefore, the $95%$ confidence interval for the population mean $\\mu $ is the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}17.7\\pm 1.960\\cdot \\frac{13}{\\sqrt{35}} \\\\ 17.7\\pm 4.307\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e5a0db8f-3180-5bd8-b70b-c378057351d5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e5a0db8f-3180-5bd8-b70b-c378057351d5" :answer-field/id #uuid "e5a0db8f-3180-5bd8-b70b-c378057351d5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-75d1d92b-2b36-54a4-b2cf-4ac256db1673" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d84092c9-3b31-552b-adfb-723bcf7fb150" "answer-b7856ac8-ec2f-50ab-bc23-6d03b87e0fa8" "answer-c982bd21-dd7a-5c4b-8ccf-4e604f9774ff" "answer-75d1d92b-2b36-54a4-b2cf-4ac256db1673" "answer-e0615d3f-e7f8-55a7-8635-ac92d296cc62"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d84092c9-3b31-552b-adfb-723bcf7fb150" :answer/id #uuid "d84092c9-3b31-552b-adfb-723bcf7fb150" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "13\\pm 3.615\\,\\text{lb}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b7856ac8-ec2f-50ab-bc23-6d03b87e0fa8" :answer/id #uuid "b7856ac8-ec2f-50ab-bc23-6d03b87e0fa8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "13\\pm 4.307\\,\\text{lb}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c982bd21-dd7a-5c4b-8ccf-4e604f9774ff" :answer/id #uuid "c982bd21-dd7a-5c4b-8ccf-4e604f9774ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "17.7\\pm 3.615\\,\\text{lb}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-75d1d92b-2b36-54a4-b2cf-4ac256db1673" :answer/id #uuid "75d1d92b-2b36-54a4-b2cf-4ac256db1673" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "17.7\\pm 4.307\\,\\text{lb}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e0615d3f-e7f8-55a7-8635-ac92d296cc62" :answer/id #uuid "e0615d3f-e7f8-55a7-8635-ac92d296cc62" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "17.7\\pm 5.661\\,\\text{lb}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-b23caed2-6738-5a67-8cf1-8f3f5f29cbd3" :activity/id #uuid "b23caed2-6738-5a67-8cf1-8f3f5f29cbd3" :activity/title "Confidence Intervals for One Mean: Known Population Variance" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186050921 :activity/course 17592186046644 :activity/steps ["step-5ae1c49f-ac9b-5137-80ce-bf2b191de428" "step-6b7f3bb3-b1ad-5d58-b892-d4f2e373d33c" "step-8ab712a3-0c74-5547-b865-acd7fb2afd25" "step-ce2405e8-18b7-5ace-94c6-778401fcddf3" "step-c5f43226-e606-5921-9ff9-fcffde1df948"] :activity/first-step "step-5ae1c49f-ac9b-5137-80ce-bf2b191de428" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-5ae1c49f-ac9b-5137-80ce-bf2b191de428" :step/id #uuid "5ae1c49f-ac9b-5137-80ce-bf2b191de428" :step/content "question-43b89dfd-2b90-59a8-92b5-edcb02011dcc" :step/next "step-6b7f3bb3-b1ad-5d58-b892-d4f2e373d33c" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-6b7f3bb3-b1ad-5d58-b892-d4f2e373d33c" :step/id #uuid "6b7f3bb3-b1ad-5d58-b892-d4f2e373d33c" :step/content "question-6b59066d-5e7f-5521-a647-a4e84084b17c" :step/next "step-8ab712a3-0c74-5547-b865-acd7fb2afd25" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-8ab712a3-0c74-5547-b865-acd7fb2afd25" :step/id #uuid "8ab712a3-0c74-5547-b865-acd7fb2afd25" :step/content 17592186499548 :step/next "step-ce2405e8-18b7-5ace-94c6-778401fcddf3" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-ce2405e8-18b7-5ace-94c6-778401fcddf3" :step/id #uuid "ce2405e8-18b7-5ace-94c6-778401fcddf3" :step/content "question-d4daf7f4-d328-5530-aaf2-46c1276ac650" :step/next "step-c5f43226-e606-5921-9ff9-fcffde1df948" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-c5f43226-e606-5921-9ff9-fcffde1df948" :step/id #uuid "c5f43226-e606-5921-9ff9-fcffde1df948" :step/content 17592186499443 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186375288 :answer-field/choices 17592186375289] [:db/retract 17592186375288 :answer-field/choices 17592186375290] [:db/retract 17592186375288 :answer-field/choices 17592186375291] [:db/retract 17592186375288 :answer-field/choices 17592186375292] [:db/retract 17592186375288 :answer-field/choices 17592186375293] [:db/retract 17592186129840 :question/answer-fields 17592186128521] [:db/retract 17592186341458 :answer-field/choices 17592186341299] [:db/retract 17592186341458 :answer-field/choices 17592186340197] [:db/retract 17592186341458 :answer-field/choices 17592186339386] [:db/retract 17592186341458 :answer-field/choices 17592186340125] [:db/retract 17592186341458 :answer-field/choices 17592186339183] {:db/id 17592186129840 :question/worked-solution "A type II region can be written as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,a\\le y\\le b,\\,g(y)\\le x\\le f(y)\\},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nTo express the given region as a type II region, we first rewrite all of the given curves as functions of $y:$\n\n$$\ny=2x\\,⟹\\,x=\\frac{y}{2}\n$$\n\nThe function $x=\\sqrt{y}+1$ is already written as a function of $y.$\n\nNotice that the region lies between the horizontal lines $y=1$ and $y=4.$ So, we have $1\\le y\\le 4.$\n\nWe draw a horizontal arrow through the region to determine the left function $g(y)$ and the right function $f(y).$ A horizontal line should intersect the region in a single interval only for it to be a type II region.\n\n![](images/c5/c55d5f809462b767122ccc4af97c5b4d243730ed24f655bdc18e35ec57e25ce2.png)\n\nThe horizontal line enters the region through the lower function $x=\\frac{y}{2}$ and leaves through the upper function $x=\\sqrt{y}+1.$ So, we have $\\frac{y}{2}\\le x\\le \\sqrt{y}+1.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 4,\\,\\frac{y}{2}\\le x\\le \\sqrt{y}+1\\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186375288 :answer-field/correct "answer-f038c740-7bd9-542c-aa85-3c158363caa4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-98af0664-fef3-5195-8942-4ae62f79f459" "answer-86e11a1f-00dc-51de-8fae-8e31288e9455" "answer-f038c740-7bd9-542c-aa85-3c158363caa4" "answer-a5a1af78-5337-58fe-9506-fb9b3db058f1" "answer-9f3d9aa4-b230-5307-8b9e-8fda1b89d36a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-98af0664-fef3-5195-8942-4ae62f79f459" :answer/id #uuid "98af0664-fef3-5195-8942-4ae62f79f459" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 4,\\,2y\\le x\\le \\sqrt{y}+1\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-86e11a1f-00dc-51de-8fae-8e31288e9455" :answer/id #uuid "86e11a1f-00dc-51de-8fae-8e31288e9455" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 4,\\,2y\\le x\\le \\sqrt{y}\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f038c740-7bd9-542c-aa85-3c158363caa4" :answer/id #uuid "f038c740-7bd9-542c-aa85-3c158363caa4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 4,\\,\\frac{y}{2}\\le x\\le \\sqrt{y}+1\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a5a1af78-5337-58fe-9506-fb9b3db058f1" :answer/id #uuid "a5a1af78-5337-58fe-9506-fb9b3db058f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\frac{1}{2}\\le x\\le 2\\,,\\,2x\\le y\\le (x-1)^{2}\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9f3d9aa4-b230-5307-8b9e-8fda1b89d36a" :answer/id #uuid "9f3d9aa4-b230-5307-8b9e-8fda1b89d36a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\frac{1}{2}\\le x\\le 3\\,,\\,2x\\le y\\le \\sqrt{x}+1\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186375321 :question/worked-solution "A type II region can be written as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,a\\le y\\le b,\\,g(y)\\le x\\le f(y)\\},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nA type II region has the property that a horizontal line drawn through the region intersects the region in a single interval only.\n\nAmong the given options, the only type II region is the following.\n\n![](images/12/1206abdf317df09c8c54714a6178d78570b3c10a49513c3c626c09be3ea2cf72.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186342005 :question/worked-solution "A type II region can be written as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,a\\le y\\le b,\\,g(y)\\le x\\le f(y)\\},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nTo express the given region as a type II region, we first rewrite all of the given curves as functions of $y:$\n\n$$\ny=-2(x-3)\\,⟹\\,x=-\\frac{y}{2}+3\n$$\n\nThe function $x=-\\sqrt{y}+2$ is already written as a function of $y.$\n\nNotice that the region lies between the horizontal lines $y=1$ and $y=3.$ So, we have $1\\le y\\le 3.$\n\nWe draw a horizontal arrow through the region to determine the left function $g(y)$ and the right function $f(y).$ A horizontal line should intersect the region in a single interval only for it to be a type II region.\n\n![](images/fb/fb05eec73599c1beb8dd588c478208315f6edaf10af999115eb29fa10d5601e9.png)\n\nThe horizontal line enters the region through the lower function $x=-\\sqrt{y}+2$ and leaves through the upper function $x=-\\frac{y}{2}+3.$ So, we have $-\\sqrt{y}+2\\le x\\le -\\frac{y}{2}+3.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 3,\\,-\\sqrt{y}+2\\le x\\le -\\frac{y}{2}+3\\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186341458 :answer-field/correct "answer-a8039587-077a-5341-9003-3971e08c6ca6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b4fa72f4-3cd9-588c-8d31-a887a4ecafd6" "answer-f6ff3e83-5d71-5daa-b2f8-25c47f45a202" "answer-a8039587-077a-5341-9003-3971e08c6ca6" "answer-1756c48c-665f-5f06-b577-1b909cc87f92" "answer-1a8d8801-ef97-55e2-bc3a-31cf1be29d3f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b4fa72f4-3cd9-588c-8d31-a887a4ecafd6" :answer/id #uuid "b4fa72f4-3cd9-588c-8d31-a887a4ecafd6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-\\sqrt{y}+2\\le y\\le -\\frac{y}{2}+3,\\,1\\le x\\le 3\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f6ff3e83-5d71-5daa-b2f8-25c47f45a202" :answer/id #uuid "f6ff3e83-5d71-5daa-b2f8-25c47f45a202" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 3,\\,-\\sqrt{y}+2\\le x\\le 2.5\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a8039587-077a-5341-9003-3971e08c6ca6" :answer/id #uuid "a8039587-077a-5341-9003-3971e08c6ca6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 3,\\,-\\sqrt{y}+2\\le x\\le -\\frac{y}{2}+3\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1756c48c-665f-5f06-b577-1b909cc87f92" :answer/id #uuid "1756c48c-665f-5f06-b577-1b909cc87f92" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 3,\\,-\\sqrt{y}+3\\le x\\le \\frac{y}{2}+2\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1a8d8801-ef97-55e2-bc3a-31cf1be29d3f" :answer/id #uuid "1a8d8801-ef97-55e2-bc3a-31cf1be29d3f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\sqrt{y}\\le y\\le \\frac{y}{2},\\,1\\le x\\le 3\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-820c7569-ca59-5a59-b866-f834cfa94ce3" :activity/id #uuid "820c7569-ca59-5a59-b866-f834cfa94ce3" :activity/title "Type I and II Regions in Two-Dimensional Space" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186050822 :activity/course 17592186046658 :activity/steps ["step-1eccfbc0-5646-515c-b76e-a435267876f8" "step-549657be-a51d-5365-b225-95d098f92f33" "step-b5cb88a3-789d-5dd8-871d-8cd73e60f6f0" "step-d98b72e4-43cf-558b-8b0e-212ac545b3e9" "step-0d43dfd0-0bc2-522d-9f41-53b137a34a58"] :activity/first-step "step-1eccfbc0-5646-515c-b76e-a435267876f8" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-1eccfbc0-5646-515c-b76e-a435267876f8" :step/id #uuid "1eccfbc0-5646-515c-b76e-a435267876f8" :step/content 17592186129840 :step/next "step-549657be-a51d-5365-b225-95d098f92f33" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-549657be-a51d-5365-b225-95d098f92f33" :step/id #uuid "549657be-a51d-5365-b225-95d098f92f33" :step/content 17592186129842 :step/next "step-b5cb88a3-789d-5dd8-871d-8cd73e60f6f0" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-b5cb88a3-789d-5dd8-871d-8cd73e60f6f0" :step/id #uuid "b5cb88a3-789d-5dd8-871d-8cd73e60f6f0" :step/content 17592186375321 :step/next "step-d98b72e4-43cf-558b-8b0e-212ac545b3e9" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-d98b72e4-43cf-558b-8b0e-212ac545b3e9" :step/id #uuid "d98b72e4-43cf-558b-8b0e-212ac545b3e9" :step/content 17592186342005 :step/next "step-0d43dfd0-0bc2-522d-9f41-53b137a34a58" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-0d43dfd0-0bc2-522d-9f41-53b137a34a58" :step/id #uuid "0d43dfd0-0bc2-522d-9f41-53b137a34a58" :step/content 17592186342012 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054739 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-a2cc15c9-6ca6-5c2d-9f16-f12bfe047553" "question-dd3c4104-b695-59fd-871c-afa5ad204e67"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054566 :question/problem "Solve $f(x)=0,$ where $f(x) = \\dfrac{2x + 1}{x^2 + x - 6}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor $f(x),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{2x+1}{{x}^{2}+x-6} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x+1}{(x+3)(x-2)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThere are no common factors in the numerator and denominator, so we set the numerator equal to zero and solve for $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+1 & =0 \\\\ 2x & =-1 \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to $f(x)=0$ is $x=-\\dfrac{1}{2}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054740 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-19bba278-dfe5-5c03-8d05-5a3c3649901e" "question-f03d8bec-d8c1-5f5b-8e78-5d11e09f4352"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054555 :question/problem "Solve $f(x)=0,$ where $f(x) = \\dfrac{x^2-4x}{x^2+5x+6}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor $f(x),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{{x}^{2}-4x}{{x}^{2}+5x+6} \\\\  & =\\frac{x(x-4)}{(x+2)(x+3)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere are no common factors in the numerator and denominator, so we set the numerator equal to zero and solve for $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(x-4) & =0 \\\\ x & =0,4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions to $f(x)=0$ are $x=0$ and $x=4.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054741 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-35ce6eb4-991f-5d5d-bf8d-bb7ed13aec66" "question-60c93613-0dc8-54aa-a9e0-7ec27315eb60"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054554 :question/problem "Solve $f(x)=0,$ where $f(x) = \\dfrac{x+1}{x^2-x-2}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{x+1}{{x}^{2}-x-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{x+1}{(x+1)(x-2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{(x+1)}}{\\cancel{(x+1)}(x-2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x-2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the numerator equal to zero, we get $1=0,$ which is a false statement. Therefore, $f(x)=0$ has no solution." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054742 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-c9052e44-409b-5493-8da2-7b4975b14835" "question-ddd618d8-1530-59f2-b97b-98d26b79c22a" "question-8460a1ed-5635-5121-961a-4a208d9777ff" "question-88464372-728b-5e12-ab3a-004869808716"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054556 :question/problem "Solve $f(x)=0$, where $f(x) = \\dfrac{x^3-2x^2-9x+18}{x^2-x-2}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-9x+18}{{x}^{2}-x-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}(x-2)-9(x-2)}{(x-2)(x+1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x-2)({x}^{2}-9)}{(x-2)(x+1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x-2)(x-3)(x+3)}{(x-2)(x+1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{(x-2)}(x-3)(x+3)}{\\cancel{(x-2)}(x+1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x-3)(x+3)}{x+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the numerator equal to zero and solving for $x$ gives\n\n$$\n(x-3)(x+3) = 0 \\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad x = \\pm3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions to $f(x)=0$ are $x=3$ and $x=-3.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-a2cc15c9-6ca6-5c2d-9f16-f12bfe047553" :question/id #uuid "a2cc15c9-6ca6-5c2d-9f16-f12bfe047553" :question/math-academy-id "q-113062" :question/problem "Solve $f(x)=0$ where $f(x)=\\frac{x+5}{2{x}^{2}-5x-25}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor $f(x),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{x+5}{2{x}^{2}-5x-25} \\\\  & =\\frac{x+5}{(x-5)(2x+5)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThere are no common factors in the numerator and denominator, so we set the numerator equal to zero and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+5 & =0 \\\\ x & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to $f(x)=0$ is $x=-5.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-bcea6cf5-7717-5f7d-aee1-c92728386a3c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-bcea6cf5-7717-5f7d-aee1-c92728386a3c" :answer-field/id #uuid "bcea6cf5-7717-5f7d-aee1-c92728386a3c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-849f979a-f3f5-53e7-b5cd-260cb22f029e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-849f979a-f3f5-53e7-b5cd-260cb22f029e" "answer-ef848463-b168-563e-9883-b757267bfe81" "answer-4b375d78-a87f-59d3-9572-b17e9d856299" "answer-54bdfb8e-a045-5d76-b2e2-d543a6fcf2e5" "answer-53cf8488-82bd-5c40-a7af-14f82f5ba4f4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-849f979a-f3f5-53e7-b5cd-260cb22f029e" :answer/id #uuid "849f979a-f3f5-53e7-b5cd-260cb22f029e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ef848463-b168-563e-9883-b757267bfe81" :answer/id #uuid "ef848463-b168-563e-9883-b757267bfe81" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-\\frac{5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4b375d78-a87f-59d3-9572-b17e9d856299" :answer/id #uuid "4b375d78-a87f-59d3-9572-b17e9d856299" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-54bdfb8e-a045-5d76-b2e2-d543a6fcf2e5" :answer/id #uuid "54bdfb8e-a045-5d76-b2e2-d543a6fcf2e5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-53cf8488-82bd-5c40-a7af-14f82f5ba4f4" :answer/id #uuid "53cf8488-82bd-5c40-a7af-14f82f5ba4f4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The equation has no solution" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-dd3c4104-b695-59fd-871c-afa5ad204e67" :question/id #uuid "dd3c4104-b695-59fd-871c-afa5ad204e67" :question/math-academy-id "q-70499" :question/problem "Solve $f(t)=0$ where $f(t)=\\frac{t-3}{{t}^{2}+6t+5}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor $f(t),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =\\frac{t-3}{{t}^{2}+6t+5} \\\\  & =\\frac{t-3}{(t+5)(t+1)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThere are no common factors in the numerator and denominator, so we set the numerator equal to zero and solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t-3 & =0 \\\\ t & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to $f(t)=0$ is $t=3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4d83edb1-1f8c-5230-883b-d0994ae0440d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4d83edb1-1f8c-5230-883b-d0994ae0440d" :answer-field/id #uuid "4d83edb1-1f8c-5230-883b-d0994ae0440d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-af1622c7-40b8-5bd4-8e78-9857f18ace03" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d7b1d9a3-0101-5ff1-aa74-6f16ed44bf13" "answer-8f557bac-7bbb-5a6b-9ece-8401b03a9e75" "answer-af1622c7-40b8-5bd4-8e78-9857f18ace03" "answer-167d4b9b-b6e5-52dc-b8f7-bf49a917fdb7" "answer-862a142c-3d12-5829-8961-607a133af512"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d7b1d9a3-0101-5ff1-aa74-6f16ed44bf13" :answer/id #uuid "d7b1d9a3-0101-5ff1-aa74-6f16ed44bf13" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8f557bac-7bbb-5a6b-9ece-8401b03a9e75" :answer/id #uuid "8f557bac-7bbb-5a6b-9ece-8401b03a9e75" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-af1622c7-40b8-5bd4-8e78-9857f18ace03" :answer/id #uuid "af1622c7-40b8-5bd4-8e78-9857f18ace03" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-167d4b9b-b6e5-52dc-b8f7-bf49a917fdb7" :answer/id #uuid "167d4b9b-b6e5-52dc-b8f7-bf49a917fdb7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-862a142c-3d12-5829-8961-607a133af512" :answer/id #uuid "862a142c-3d12-5829-8961-607a133af512" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The equation has no solution" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-19bba278-dfe5-5c03-8d05-5a3c3649901e" :question/id #uuid "19bba278-dfe5-5c03-8d05-5a3c3649901e" :question/math-academy-id "q-25301" :question/problem "Find the roots of $f(w)=\\frac{{w}^{2}-w-2}{w-5}.$" :question/worked-solution "The roots of $f(w)$ are the solutions to the equation $f(w)=0.$ In our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{{w}^{2}-w-2}{w-5}=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we factor $f(w),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(w) & =\\frac{{w}^{2}-w-2}{w-5} \\\\  & =\\frac{(w-2)(w+1)}{w-5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere are no common factors in the numerator and denominator, so we set the numerator equal to zero and solve for $w:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(w-2)(w+1) & =0 \\\\ w & =-1,\\,2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions to $f(w)=0$ are $w=-1$ and $w=2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b0ef1040-77da-560a-87d7-15632abbe381"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b0ef1040-77da-560a-87d7-15632abbe381" :answer-field/id #uuid "b0ef1040-77da-560a-87d7-15632abbe381" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-377800ac-d02d-5ee7-9054-9beacb06ab2b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-377800ac-d02d-5ee7-9054-9beacb06ab2b" "answer-9e873323-4894-55fb-b9e3-3c4721bcb462" "answer-6b18dd16-63d0-56e3-a6ab-4af8268e8f23" "answer-4df9e14b-ce47-5984-8b22-2b57b89d6d13" "answer-f2919458-4ec2-5e45-beec-98e5b60984fb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-377800ac-d02d-5ee7-9054-9beacb06ab2b" :answer/id #uuid "377800ac-d02d-5ee7-9054-9beacb06ab2b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "w=-1,\\,2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9e873323-4894-55fb-b9e3-3c4721bcb462" :answer/id #uuid "9e873323-4894-55fb-b9e3-3c4721bcb462" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "w=-1,\\,4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6b18dd16-63d0-56e3-a6ab-4af8268e8f23" :answer/id #uuid "6b18dd16-63d0-56e3-a6ab-4af8268e8f23" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "w=-2,\\,1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4df9e14b-ce47-5984-8b22-2b57b89d6d13" :answer/id #uuid "4df9e14b-ce47-5984-8b22-2b57b89d6d13" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "w=-3,\\,2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f2919458-4ec2-5e45-beec-98e5b60984fb" :answer/id #uuid "f2919458-4ec2-5e45-beec-98e5b60984fb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No real roots" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-f03d8bec-d8c1-5f5b-8e78-5d11e09f4352" :question/id #uuid "f03d8bec-d8c1-5f5b-8e78-5d11e09f4352" :question/math-academy-id "q-277862" :question/problem "In **ascending order**, the roots of $g(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}-16}{{x}^{2}-7x+10}$ are\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$\nand\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "The roots of $g(x)$ are the solutions to the equation $g(x)=0.$ In our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}-16}{{x}^{2}-7x+10}=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we factor $g(x),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(x) & =\\frac{{x}^{2}-16}{{x}^{2}-7x+10} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+4)(x-4)}{(x-2)(x-5)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere are no common factors in the numerator and denominator, so we set the numerator equal to zero and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+4)(x-4) & =0 \\\\ x & =-4,\\,4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions to $g(x)=0$, in ascending order, are $x=-4$ and $x=4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6f6715e4-b16a-58f4-9041-8f3d0e03cf18" "answer-field-78c8b077-e976-516b-8732-4f6c3a8a52fe"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6f6715e4-b16a-58f4-9041-8f3d0e03cf18" :answer-field/id #uuid "6f6715e4-b16a-58f4-9041-8f3d0e03cf18" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-ceeefb89-cfe9-5b37-9bbc-39109065eb8d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ceeefb89-cfe9-5b37-9bbc-39109065eb8d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ceeefb89-cfe9-5b37-9bbc-39109065eb8d" :answer/id #uuid "ceeefb89-cfe9-5b37-9bbc-39109065eb8d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-78c8b077-e976-516b-8732-4f6c3a8a52fe" :answer-field/id #uuid "78c8b077-e976-516b-8732-4f6c3a8a52fe" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-2f31b0c1-0fac-5fda-9fee-b63a90c2d43a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2f31b0c1-0fac-5fda-9fee-b63a90c2d43a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2f31b0c1-0fac-5fda-9fee-b63a90c2d43a" :answer/id #uuid "2f31b0c1-0fac-5fda-9fee-b63a90c2d43a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-35ce6eb4-991f-5d5d-bf8d-bb7ed13aec66" :question/id #uuid "35ce6eb4-991f-5d5d-bf8d-bb7ed13aec66" :question/math-academy-id "q-270847" :question/problem "Find the roots of $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}-9x+14}{{x}^{2}-4}.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The roots of $f(x)$ are the solutions to the equation $f(x)=0.$ In our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}-9x+14}{{x}^{2}-4}=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{{x}^{2}-9x+14}{{x}^{2}-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x-7)(x-2)}{(x+2)(x-2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x-7)\\cancel{(x-2)}}{(x+2)\\cancel{(x-2)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{x-7}{x+2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the numerator equal to zero and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-7 & =0\\,⟹\\,x=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to $f(x)=0$ is $x=7.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e7fb947e-e267-5840-8345-72d0ea80120c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e7fb947e-e267-5840-8345-72d0ea80120c" :answer-field/id #uuid "e7fb947e-e267-5840-8345-72d0ea80120c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-637f3eea-aba7-5bc5-b49d-12225df44666" :answer-field/choices ["answer-637f3eea-aba7-5bc5-b49d-12225df44666"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-637f3eea-aba7-5bc5-b49d-12225df44666" :answer/id #uuid "637f3eea-aba7-5bc5-b49d-12225df44666" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-60c93613-0dc8-54aa-a9e0-7ec27315eb60" :question/id #uuid "60c93613-0dc8-54aa-a9e0-7ec27315eb60" :question/math-academy-id "q-113088" :question/problem "Find the roots of $f(z)=\\frac{{z}^{2}+5z+4}{{z}^{2}+4z}.$" :question/worked-solution "The roots of $f(z)$ are the solutions to the equation $f(z)=0.$ In our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{{z}^{2}+5z+4}{{z}^{2}+4z}=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(z) & =\\frac{{z}^{2}+5z+4}{{z}^{2}+4z} \\\\  & =\\frac{(z+1)(z+4)}{z(z+4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(z+1)\\cancel{(z+4)}}{z\\cancel{(z+4)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(z+1)}{z}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the numerator equal to zero and solve for $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z+1 & =0\\,⟹\\,z=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to $f(z)=0$ is $z=-1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a18f4ead-179e-5865-b01c-c77ce604e10d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a18f4ead-179e-5865-b01c-c77ce604e10d" :answer-field/id #uuid "a18f4ead-179e-5865-b01c-c77ce604e10d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7855cd61-3ce4-59af-aa08-15f52848df6c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7855cd61-3ce4-59af-aa08-15f52848df6c" "answer-8c0ac787-d0ae-5c5f-8b63-b275aac416bf" "answer-784e53da-ac7d-5028-9968-a4631f4feaf2" "answer-43ee574a-8a30-5b2a-b163-e85baed477ca" "answer-08bdec83-c6ad-5c2f-8191-80fcaec9c8f0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7855cd61-3ce4-59af-aa08-15f52848df6c" :answer/id #uuid "7855cd61-3ce4-59af-aa08-15f52848df6c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8c0ac787-d0ae-5c5f-8b63-b275aac416bf" :answer/id #uuid "8c0ac787-d0ae-5c5f-8b63-b275aac416bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=-4,-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-784e53da-ac7d-5028-9968-a4631f4feaf2" :answer/id #uuid "784e53da-ac7d-5028-9968-a4631f4feaf2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=0,1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-43ee574a-8a30-5b2a-b163-e85baed477ca" :answer/id #uuid "43ee574a-8a30-5b2a-b163-e85baed477ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-08bdec83-c6ad-5c2f-8191-80fcaec9c8f0" :answer/id #uuid "08bdec83-c6ad-5c2f-8191-80fcaec9c8f0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No roots" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-c9052e44-409b-5493-8da2-7b4975b14835" :question/id #uuid "c9052e44-409b-5493-8da2-7b4975b14835" :question/math-academy-id "q-25299" :question/problem "Find the roots of $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}+x-20}{{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-9x+18}.$" :question/worked-solution "The roots of $f(x)$ are the solutions to the equation $f(x)=0.$ In our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}+x-20}{{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-9x+18}=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{{x}^{2}+x-20}{{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-9x+18} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+5)(x-4)}{{x}^{2}(x-2)-9(x-2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+5)(x-4)}{({x}^{2}-9)(x-2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+5)(x-4)}{(x+3)(x-3)(x-2)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the numerator equal to zero and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+5)(x-4)=0\\,⟹\\,x=-5,\\,4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to $f(x)=0$ are $x=-5$ and $x=4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-85571c32-e16c-59f6-ab7a-5ad637ae9027"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-85571c32-e16c-59f6-ab7a-5ad637ae9027" :answer-field/id #uuid "85571c32-e16c-59f6-ab7a-5ad637ae9027" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1c681bc2-db89-5b8b-a888-6e454a854953" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f109c122-ed91-5e73-a873-73bb3ed90155" "answer-cef1acc7-0b8d-5cee-81e8-42810d42b824" "answer-1c681bc2-db89-5b8b-a888-6e454a854953" "answer-0212f041-3e0f-56b5-9183-937e4d9b010f" "answer-d52afbe6-85e4-50b9-9547-01474e5a8221"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f109c122-ed91-5e73-a873-73bb3ed90155" :answer/id #uuid "f109c122-ed91-5e73-a873-73bb3ed90155" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cef1acc7-0b8d-5cee-81e8-42810d42b824" :answer/id #uuid "cef1acc7-0b8d-5cee-81e8-42810d42b824" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-5,\\,2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1c681bc2-db89-5b8b-a888-6e454a854953" :answer/id #uuid "1c681bc2-db89-5b8b-a888-6e454a854953" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-5,\\,4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0212f041-3e0f-56b5-9183-937e4d9b010f" :answer/id #uuid "0212f041-3e0f-56b5-9183-937e4d9b010f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d52afbe6-85e4-50b9-9547-01474e5a8221" :answer/id #uuid "d52afbe6-85e4-50b9-9547-01474e5a8221" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-ddd618d8-1530-59f2-b97b-98d26b79c22a" :question/id #uuid "ddd618d8-1530-59f2-b97b-98d26b79c22a" :question/math-academy-id "q-25307" :question/problem "Find the roots of $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}+3x-10}{{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-9x+18}.$" :question/worked-solution "The roots of $f(x)$ are the solutions to the equation $f(x)=0.$ In our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}+3x-10}{{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-9x+18}=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{{x}^{2}+3x-10}{{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-9x+18} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+5)(x-2)}{{x}^{2}(x-2)-9(x-2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+5)(x-2)}{({x}^{2}-9)(x-2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+5)(x-2)}{(x+3)(x-3)(x-2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+5)\\cancel{(x-2)}}{(x+3)(x-3)\\cancel{(x-2)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+5)}{(x+3)(x-3)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the numerator equal to zero and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+5=0\\,⟹\\,x=-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to $f(x)=0$ is $x=-5.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6467ad98-5aba-5b91-be20-bcc574e8fa7e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6467ad98-5aba-5b91-be20-bcc574e8fa7e" :answer-field/id #uuid "6467ad98-5aba-5b91-be20-bcc574e8fa7e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e3e0ad3e-39e3-5115-b2ac-b21b4654024e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e3e0ad3e-39e3-5115-b2ac-b21b4654024e" "answer-8ebd7bf8-010c-5124-aefb-f8446638f67b" "answer-d2473aef-b55a-5e58-afc4-eed2722a8015" "answer-ea763d4b-09e3-5e5c-b191-0925974ea72f" "answer-77453159-e112-56b2-8504-5b0644f70b41"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e3e0ad3e-39e3-5115-b2ac-b21b4654024e" :answer/id #uuid "e3e0ad3e-39e3-5115-b2ac-b21b4654024e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8ebd7bf8-010c-5124-aefb-f8446638f67b" :answer/id #uuid "8ebd7bf8-010c-5124-aefb-f8446638f67b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-5,\\,2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d2473aef-b55a-5e58-afc4-eed2722a8015" :answer/id #uuid "d2473aef-b55a-5e58-afc4-eed2722a8015" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-5,\\,3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ea763d4b-09e3-5e5c-b191-0925974ea72f" :answer/id #uuid "ea763d4b-09e3-5e5c-b191-0925974ea72f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-77453159-e112-56b2-8504-5b0644f70b41" :answer/id #uuid "77453159-e112-56b2-8504-5b0644f70b41" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-8460a1ed-5635-5121-961a-4a208d9777ff" :question/id #uuid "8460a1ed-5635-5121-961a-4a208d9777ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-278034" :question/problem "In **ascending order**, the roots of $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-x+2}{3x-3}$ are\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}} $\\,$\nand\n$\\,\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "The roots of $f(x)$ are the solutions to the equation $f(x)=0.$ In our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-x+2}{3x-3}=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-x+2}{3x-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}(x-2)-1(x-2)}{3x-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{({x}^{2}-1)(x-2)}{3(x-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x-1)(x+1)(x-2)}{3(x-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{(x-1)}(x+1)(x-2)}{3\\cancel{(x-1)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+1)(x-2)}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the numerator equal to zero and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+1)(x-2) & =0 \\\\ x & =-1,\\,2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions to $f(x)=0$, in ascending order, are $x=-1$ and $x=2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c4543e63-f861-5762-bec4-80e1b6d0937b" "answer-field-2090e862-943c-54e8-bc45-27edfeefbaac"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c4543e63-f861-5762-bec4-80e1b6d0937b" :answer-field/id #uuid "c4543e63-f861-5762-bec4-80e1b6d0937b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-9be7cb15-5f79-511e-9d04-e09b5b217932" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9be7cb15-5f79-511e-9d04-e09b5b217932"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9be7cb15-5f79-511e-9d04-e09b5b217932" :answer/id #uuid "9be7cb15-5f79-511e-9d04-e09b5b217932" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2090e862-943c-54e8-bc45-27edfeefbaac" :answer-field/id #uuid "2090e862-943c-54e8-bc45-27edfeefbaac" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-fb061fbc-28bf-5b2a-84b8-eec238396424" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fb061fbc-28bf-5b2a-84b8-eec238396424"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fb061fbc-28bf-5b2a-84b8-eec238396424" :answer/id #uuid "fb061fbc-28bf-5b2a-84b8-eec238396424" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-88464372-728b-5e12-ab3a-004869808716" :question/id #uuid "88464372-728b-5e12-ab3a-004869808716" :question/math-academy-id "q-25312" :question/problem "Find the roots of $f(h)=\\frac{{h}^{2}+9h+20}{{h}^{3}+3{h}^{2}-25h-75}.$" :question/worked-solution "The roots of $f(h)$ are the solutions to the equation $f(h)=0.$ In our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{{h}^{2}+9h+20}{{h}^{3}+3{h}^{2}-25h-75}=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(h) & =\\frac{{h}^{2}+9h+20}{{h}^{3}+3{h}^{2}-25h-75} \\\\  & =\\frac{(h+5)(h+4)}{{h}^{2}(h+3)-25(h+3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(h+5)(h+4)}{({h}^{2}-25)(h+3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(h+5)(h+4)}{(h+5)(h-5)(h+3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{(h+5)}(h+4)}{\\cancel{(h+5)}(h-5)(h+3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{h+4}{(h-5)(h+3)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the numerator equal to zero and solve for $h:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h+4=0\\,⟹\\,h=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to $f(h)=0$ is $h=-4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-dfc3d8a5-cbd4-5701-af7e-3598dbd3e3f2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-dfc3d8a5-cbd4-5701-af7e-3598dbd3e3f2" :answer-field/id #uuid "dfc3d8a5-cbd4-5701-af7e-3598dbd3e3f2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-48b461e7-6fb0-560a-8a73-95106caf3b32" :answer-field/choices ["answer-48b461e7-6fb0-560a-8a73-95106caf3b32" "answer-235c68a8-d1a1-5979-b0d4-01b41af330ad" "answer-0cb3ffc0-7e51-564d-b7d4-590f967566e0" "answer-3d6c5120-1dd4-5bd1-8211-11cd0fdf9e37" "answer-84c1c219-bfe2-5e58-a44f-84da5210e4da"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-48b461e7-6fb0-560a-8a73-95106caf3b32" :answer/id #uuid "48b461e7-6fb0-560a-8a73-95106caf3b32" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "h=-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-235c68a8-d1a1-5979-b0d4-01b41af330ad" :answer/id #uuid "235c68a8-d1a1-5979-b0d4-01b41af330ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "h=-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0cb3ffc0-7e51-564d-b7d4-590f967566e0" :answer/id #uuid "0cb3ffc0-7e51-564d-b7d4-590f967566e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "h=-5,\\,-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3d6c5120-1dd4-5bd1-8211-11cd0fdf9e37" :answer/id #uuid "3d6c5120-1dd4-5bd1-8211-11cd0fdf9e37" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "h=4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-84c1c219-bfe2-5e58-a44f-84da5210e4da" :answer/id #uuid "84c1c219-bfe2-5e58-a44f-84da5210e4da" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "h=4,\\,5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186055979 :tutorial/content "To find the zeros of a rational function, we first need to factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors. Then, we set the numerator equal to zero and solve.\n\nFor example, consider the function $f(x) = \\dfrac{x-3}{x^2-25}.$ Factoring the numerator and denominator, we get\n\n$$\nf(x) = \\dfrac{x-3}{(x+5)(x-5)}.\n$$\n\nThere are no common factors to cancel, so we set the numerator equal to zero and solve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-3 & =0 \\\\ x & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to $f(x)=0$ is $x=3.$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054883 :activity/expected-seconds 600.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186188276 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-58e1bdfb-9550-5950-b391-e8892b95af10" "question-1e85b0be-111d-5b57-b950-c149f90f77dc"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186188536 :question/problem "Given the joint probability distribution for two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ below, find $\\text{E}[Y].$\n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ | $0.25$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.25$ | $0.15$ | $0.2$ |" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals, and the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals.\n\n| $f(x,y)$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ | $0.25$ | $…$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.25$ | $0.15$ | $0.2$ | $…$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.3$ | $0.25$ | $0.45$ | $1$ |\n\nTherefore, the probability mass function for  $Y$ is given by the following table:\n\n| $y$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.3$ | $0.25$ | $0.45$ |\n\nFinally, the  expected value of $Y$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y] & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}\\,{f}_{Y}({y}_{i}) \\\\  & =0\\cdot 0.3+1\\cdot 0.25+2\\cdot 0.45 \\\\  & =0+0.25+0.9 \\\\  & =1.15.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186185496 :answer-field/correct 17592186185497 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186188296 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-57c74959-06e0-5008-b9fc-e618f65747e4"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186188538 :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}y, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{3}{4},$ find $\\text{E}[4X+6Y].$" :question/worked-solution "We're given $\\text{E}[X].$ So, we first need to compute $\\text{E}[Y].$\n\nThe marginal density function for $Y$ when $0\\le y\\le 2$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}y[{x}^{3}]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}y({1}^{3}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{y}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the  expected value of $Y$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }y\\,{f}_{Y}(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\cdot \\frac{y}{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[{y}^{3}]_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}(8-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[4X+6Y] & =4\\,\\text{E}[X]+6\\,\\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =4(\\frac{3}{4})+6(\\frac{4}{3}) \\\\  & =3+8 \\\\  & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186185508 :answer-field/correct 17592186185511 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-57c74959-06e0-5008-b9fc-e618f65747e4" :question/id #uuid "57c74959-06e0-5008-b9fc-e618f65747e4" :question/math-academy-id "q-143584" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{9}({x}^{3}+{y}^{3}), & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that $\\text{E}[Y]=\\frac{23}{15},$ find $\\text{E}[3X-Y].$" :question/worked-solution "We're given $\\text{E}[Y].$ So, we first need to compute $\\text{E}[X].$\n\nThe marginal density function for $X$ when $0\\le x\\le 1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{2}{9}({x}^{3}+{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}{[{x}^{3}y+\\frac{{y}^{4}}{4}]}_{y=0}^{y=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}(2{x}^{3}+\\frac{{2}^{4}}{4}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}({x}^{3}+2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the  expected value of $X$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }x\\,{f}_{X}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\cdot \\frac{4}{9}({x}^{3}+2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}{\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{4}+2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}{[\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}+{x}^{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}(\\frac{1}{5}+1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{15}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[3X-Y] & =3\\,\\text{E}[X]+(-1)\\,\\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =3\\,(\\frac{8}{15})-(\\frac{23}{15}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{15}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b3819eb9-9cd0-5d3c-852e-6d38178d3c62"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b3819eb9-9cd0-5d3c-852e-6d38178d3c62" :answer-field/id #uuid "b3819eb9-9cd0-5d3c-852e-6d38178d3c62" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-bd2ebd72-45b1-5c05-82b9-a266f54fe224" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bd2ebd72-45b1-5c05-82b9-a266f54fe224" "answer-d551241c-84d6-5150-94ac-c0e6751dcdf3" "answer-9cdb3a18-70b7-5be8-85e6-7d754574d6e7" "answer-320777af-ae37-523c-bacf-e28e66480cc3" "answer-7852e317-6684-5e8f-b211-c3d2fd1b2920"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bd2ebd72-45b1-5c05-82b9-a266f54fe224" :answer/id #uuid "bd2ebd72-45b1-5c05-82b9-a266f54fe224" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{15}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d551241c-84d6-5150-94ac-c0e6751dcdf3" :answer/id #uuid "d551241c-84d6-5150-94ac-c0e6751dcdf3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9cdb3a18-70b7-5be8-85e6-7d754574d6e7" :answer/id #uuid "9cdb3a18-70b7-5be8-85e6-7d754574d6e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-320777af-ae37-523c-bacf-e28e66480cc3" :answer/id #uuid "320777af-ae37-523c-bacf-e28e66480cc3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7852e317-6684-5e8f-b211-c3d2fd1b2920" :answer/id #uuid "7852e317-6684-5e8f-b211-c3d2fd1b2920" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{15}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-58e1bdfb-9550-5950-b391-e8892b95af10" :question/id #uuid "58e1bdfb-9550-5950-b391-e8892b95af10" :question/math-academy-id "q-143604" :question/problem "Given the joint probability distribution for two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ below, find $\\text{E}[2X+4Y].$\n\n| $f$ | $Y=-2$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=-1$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ | $0.15$ | $0.05$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.05$ | $0.05$ | $0.15$ | $0.1$ |" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals, and the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=-2$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=-1$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ | $0.3$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ | $0.15$ | $0.05$ | $0.35$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.05$ | $0.05$ | $0.15$ | $0.1$ | $0.35$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.2$ | $0.2$ | $0.35$ | $0.25$ | $1$ |\n\nTherefore,  the probability mass functions for  $X$ and $Y$ are given by the following tables:\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">${f}_{X}(x)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.3$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.35$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.35$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th>\n<th width=\"50\"></th>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$y$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$4$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">${f}_{Y}(y)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.35$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.25$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nNow, we can compute the expected values for $X$ and $Y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}\\,{f}_{X}({x}_{i}) \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot 0.3+1\\cdot 0.35+3\\cdot 0.35 \\\\  & =-0.3+0.35+1.05 \\\\  & =1.1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y] & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}\\,{f}_{Y}({y}_{i}) \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot 0.2+0\\cdot 0.2+2\\cdot 0.35+4\\cdot 0.25 \\\\  & =-0.4+0+0.7+1 \\\\  & =1.3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the properties of expectation, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[2X+4Y] & =2\\text{E}[X]+4\\,\\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =2(1.1)+4(1.3) \\\\  & =2.2+5.2 \\\\  & =7.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5c3d7ec3-2b65-5d8c-8b98-80722d885c87"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5c3d7ec3-2b65-5d8c-8b98-80722d885c87" :answer-field/id #uuid "5c3d7ec3-2b65-5d8c-8b98-80722d885c87" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-221fa59d-39a2-5c91-a249-8862c6b794b6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a166d431-6741-566e-a4d1-3e91ef5f0388" "answer-a02fd45f-1410-54c4-bb64-034b16bd73d1" "answer-221fa59d-39a2-5c91-a249-8862c6b794b6" "answer-82e3153b-16a6-58ac-b3a6-8a86fae4ce60" "answer-3e0b2a8d-ea50-5575-ae8b-df8e61b4fd0a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a166d431-6741-566e-a4d1-3e91ef5f0388" :answer/id #uuid "a166d431-6741-566e-a4d1-3e91ef5f0388" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5.9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a02fd45f-1410-54c4-bb64-034b16bd73d1" :answer/id #uuid "a02fd45f-1410-54c4-bb64-034b16bd73d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-221fa59d-39a2-5c91-a249-8862c6b794b6" :answer/id #uuid "221fa59d-39a2-5c91-a249-8862c6b794b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7.4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-82e3153b-16a6-58ac-b3a6-8a86fae4ce60" :answer/id #uuid "82e3153b-16a6-58ac-b3a6-8a86fae4ce60" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9.05" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3e0b2a8d-ea50-5575-ae8b-df8e61b4fd0a" :answer/id #uuid "3e0b2a8d-ea50-5575-ae8b-df8e61b4fd0a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9.2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-1e85b0be-111d-5b57-b950-c149f90f77dc" :question/id #uuid "1e85b0be-111d-5b57-b950-c149f90f77dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-149599" :question/problem "Given the joint probability distribution for two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ below, find $\\text{E}[Y].$\n\n| $f$ | $Y=-2$ | $Y=-1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.3$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.25$ | $0.2$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ |" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals, and the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals.\n\n| $f(x,y)$ | $Y=-2$ | $Y=-1$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.3$ | $…$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.25$ | $0.2$ | $…$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ | $…$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.4$ | $0.6$ | $1$ |\n\nTherefore, the probability mass function for  $Y$ is given by the following table:\n\n| $y$ | $-2$ | $-1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.4$ | $0.6$ |\n\nFinally, the  expected value of $Y$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y] & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}\\,{f}_{Y}({y}_{i}) \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot 0.4+(-1)\\cdot 0.6 \\\\  & =-0.8-0.6 \\\\  & =-1.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c8ce17d4-130c-5b9e-a7e1-458cb727bad8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c8ce17d4-130c-5b9e-a7e1-458cb727bad8" :answer-field/id #uuid "c8ce17d4-130c-5b9e-a7e1-458cb727bad8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-54921f49-41bd-59ea-87fa-1aa8a31bf9f6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c6bc73a6-19e3-5079-8075-c87f32448b75" "answer-54921f49-41bd-59ea-87fa-1aa8a31bf9f6" "answer-8af359a3-0397-596f-9263-82e98df0c5e7" "answer-e6ed4ece-6571-5aa6-a239-9c83bba0bbb7" "answer-b6ef201f-91de-5739-8423-ca5f69f9f69b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c6bc73a6-19e3-5079-8075-c87f32448b75" :answer/id #uuid "c6bc73a6-19e3-5079-8075-c87f32448b75" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1.2" :db/e