answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e97c4d66-5268-5c26-8025-6f1540da8cb0" :question/id #uuid "e97c4d66-5268-5c26-8025-6f1540da8cb0" :question/math-academy-id "q-554" :question/problem "Simplify ${\\text{i}}^{27}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the value of $\\text{i}$ raised to some positive integer power $n$, we divide $n$ by $4,$ and raise $\\text{i}$ to the remainder.\n\nIn our case, we have $n=27.$ Dividing the power by $4,$ we get\n\n$$\n27÷4=6\\,\\text{R}3.\n$$\n\nSo the remainder is $3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{\\text{i}}^{27}={\\text{i}}^{3}=-\\text{i}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2efa9861-bd6e-570a-8910-36882db4e19c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2efa9861-bd6e-570a-8910-36882db4e19c" :answer-field/id #uuid "2efa9861-bd6e-570a-8910-36882db4e19c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-fb124c64-8723-57a9-8478-8dc10bb975e8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5447ea87-e11a-50f7-a3b8-9b12ed5741c1" "answer-fb124c64-8723-57a9-8478-8dc10bb975e8" "answer-25cf66c5-e27f-5642-9233-7fc96d6bfc68" "answer-30fe0027-51f9-5cd3-ab41-0608ddbddefb" "answer-bc81ac12-213b-58c2-a6a0-0def39e97f6c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5447ea87-e11a-50f7-a3b8-9b12ed5741c1" :answer/id #uuid "5447ea87-e11a-50f7-a3b8-9b12ed5741c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fb124c64-8723-57a9-8478-8dc10bb975e8" :answer/id #uuid "fb124c64-8723-57a9-8478-8dc10bb975e8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-25cf66c5-e27f-5642-9233-7fc96d6bfc68" :answer/id #uuid "25cf66c5-e27f-5642-9233-7fc96d6bfc68" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-30fe0027-51f9-5cd3-ab41-0608ddbddefb" :answer/id #uuid "30fe0027-51f9-5cd3-ab41-0608ddbddefb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "27" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bc81ac12-213b-58c2-a6a0-0def39e97f6c" :answer/id #uuid "bc81ac12-213b-58c2-a6a0-0def39e97f6c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-963c1f30-8cab-5b1e-a22e-507ad07f1c0a" :question/id #uuid "963c1f30-8cab-5b1e-a22e-507ad07f1c0a" :question/math-academy-id "q-921" :question/problem "What is the value of ${\\text{i}}^{7}?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the value of $\\text{i}$ raised to some positive integer power $n$, we divide $n$ by $4,$ and raise $\\text{i}$ to the remainder.\n\nIn our case, we have $n=7.$ Dividing the power by $4,$ we get\n\n$$\n7÷4=1\\,\\text{R}3.\n$$\n\nSo the remainder is $3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{\\text{i}}^{7}={\\text{i}}^{3}=-\\text{i}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-449b3727-013d-5c7f-8153-b83812f8679d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-449b3727-013d-5c7f-8153-b83812f8679d" :answer-field/id #uuid "449b3727-013d-5c7f-8153-b83812f8679d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-decacbed-d2e3-5347-ad87-711506c21f85" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8a5b9ccf-c810-596c-a480-905fc8b7511a" "answer-decacbed-d2e3-5347-ad87-711506c21f85" "answer-3f5a2ed3-aedb-53c8-b6f0-683c2740a1ce" "answer-cd6d5655-16fd-5320-b556-780a9e47d63a" "answer-d50a43db-071f-5dad-b0e5-5a3a9f03f0b3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8a5b9ccf-c810-596c-a480-905fc8b7511a" :answer/id #uuid "8a5b9ccf-c810-596c-a480-905fc8b7511a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-decacbed-d2e3-5347-ad87-711506c21f85" :answer/id #uuid "decacbed-d2e3-5347-ad87-711506c21f85" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3f5a2ed3-aedb-53c8-b6f0-683c2740a1ce" :answer/id #uuid "3f5a2ed3-aedb-53c8-b6f0-683c2740a1ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cd6d5655-16fd-5320-b556-780a9e47d63a" :answer/id #uuid "cd6d5655-16fd-5320-b556-780a9e47d63a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d50a43db-071f-5dad-b0e5-5a3a9f03f0b3" :answer/id #uuid "d50a43db-071f-5dad-b0e5-5a3a9f03f0b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a99262a6-2443-5dc5-a1ae-4680319ed028" :question/id #uuid "a99262a6-2443-5dc5-a1ae-4680319ed028" :question/math-academy-id "q-536" :question/problem "Simplify ${({\\text{i}}^{3})}^{10}.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the power law for exponents, we have\n\n$$\n{({\\text{i}}^{3})}^{10}={\\text{i}}^{3\\cdot 10}={\\text{i}}^{30}.\n$$\n\nTo find the value of $\\text{i}$ raised to some positive integer power $n$, we divide $n$ by $4,$ and raise $\\text{i}$ to the remainder.\n\nIn our case, we have $n=30.$ Dividing the power by $4,$ we get\n\n$$\n30÷4=7\\,\\text{R}2.\n$$\n\nSo the remainder is $2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{\\text{i}}^{30}={\\text{i}}^{2}=-1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-da1fc962-9c05-5d4d-a988-eca539b9fea1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-da1fc962-9c05-5d4d-a988-eca539b9fea1" :answer-field/id #uuid "da1fc962-9c05-5d4d-a988-eca539b9fea1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-150744f4-cb82-55ac-ae42-7e7c6a5fee3f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-150744f4-cb82-55ac-ae42-7e7c6a5fee3f" "answer-64bfe8c5-244a-59b9-8372-80e64714778f" "answer-17650096-45ec-54b0-9f2b-20816e3ea300" "answer-783d135f-bab5-5d5c-a98f-030e5c1d593c" "answer-6d3a3235-368d-5426-9683-c85ceff43dff"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-150744f4-cb82-55ac-ae42-7e7c6a5fee3f" :answer/id #uuid "150744f4-cb82-55ac-ae42-7e7c6a5fee3f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-64bfe8c5-244a-59b9-8372-80e64714778f" :answer/id #uuid "64bfe8c5-244a-59b9-8372-80e64714778f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-17650096-45ec-54b0-9f2b-20816e3ea300" :answer/id #uuid "17650096-45ec-54b0-9f2b-20816e3ea300" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-783d135f-bab5-5d5c-a98f-030e5c1d593c" :answer/id #uuid "783d135f-bab5-5d5c-a98f-030e5c1d593c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6d3a3235-368d-5426-9683-c85ceff43dff" :answer/id #uuid "6d3a3235-368d-5426-9683-c85ceff43dff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-ee98c1bb-35f5-5014-9747-c74bb8f7a21e" :question/id #uuid "ee98c1bb-35f5-5014-9747-c74bb8f7a21e" :question/math-academy-id "q-535" :question/problem "If $a={\\text{i}}^{5},$ then ${a}^{3}=$" :question/worked-solution "Using the power law for exponents, we have\n\n$$\n{a}^{3}={({\\text{i}}^{5})}^{3}={\\text{i}}^{5\\cdot 3}={\\text{i}}^{15}.\n$$\n\nTo find the value of $\\text{i}$ raised to some positive integer power $n$, we divide $n$ by $4,$ and raise $\\text{i}$ to the remainder.\n\nIn our case, we have $n=15.$ Dividing the power by $4,$ we get\n\n$$\n15÷4=3\\,\\text{R}3.\n$$\n\nSo the remainder is $3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{\\text{i}}^{15}={\\text{i}}^{3}=-\\text{i}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-27ba5d5c-b1ef-53f4-96da-21e0a2672d52"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-27ba5d5c-b1ef-53f4-96da-21e0a2672d52" :answer-field/id #uuid "27ba5d5c-b1ef-53f4-96da-21e0a2672d52" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-978dec03-22c3-57eb-93f3-3a45e31ea0ae" :answer-field/choices ["answer-120a71cf-8528-512a-82ff-1d95f599c730" "answer-978dec03-22c3-57eb-93f3-3a45e31ea0ae" "answer-f83fc420-b2b0-5955-bd55-fbc821765a7b" "answer-217e49f0-4369-59a0-b87d-d301db0750c1" "answer-54aacff4-92da-52fa-94b2-bd39d9d27a91"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-120a71cf-8528-512a-82ff-1d95f599c730" :answer/id #uuid "120a71cf-8528-512a-82ff-1d95f599c730" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-978dec03-22c3-57eb-93f3-3a45e31ea0ae" :answer/id #uuid "978dec03-22c3-57eb-93f3-3a45e31ea0ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f83fc420-b2b0-5955-bd55-fbc821765a7b" :answer/id #uuid "f83fc420-b2b0-5955-bd55-fbc821765a7b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-217e49f0-4369-59a0-b87d-d301db0750c1" :answer/id #uuid "217e49f0-4369-59a0-b87d-d301db0750c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-54aacff4-92da-52fa-94b2-bd39d9d27a91" :answer/id #uuid "54aacff4-92da-52fa-94b2-bd39d9d27a91" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-fd293abd-5e28-58d2-85df-2177162157d2" :question/id #uuid "fd293abd-5e28-58d2-85df-2177162157d2" :question/math-academy-id "q-66484" :question/problem "$-5{\\text{i}}^{-1}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, using the laws of exponents, we can write\n\n$$\n-5{\\text{i}}^{-1}=-\\frac{5}{\\text{i}}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the numerator and denominator by $\\text{i},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{5}{\\text{i}}=-\\frac{5}{\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{i}}{\\text{i}}=-\\frac{5\\text{i}}{{\\text{i}}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now recall that ${\\text{i}}^{2}=-1.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n-\\frac{5\\text{i}}{{\\text{i}}^{2}}=-\\frac{5\\text{i}}{(-1)}=-\\frac{5}{(-1)}\\cdot \\text{i}=5\\text{i}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b22a68bf-48b5-5b55-b3d4-8c326751eadf"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b22a68bf-48b5-5b55-b3d4-8c326751eadf" :answer-field/id #uuid "b22a68bf-48b5-5b55-b3d4-8c326751eadf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-dc0f5c3c-5409-5295-8b20-7a4804f5c5b8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-00d2f4f8-927e-5d9b-a303-a838ea7066a1" "answer-270d63ee-8d9e-556e-a5bb-984b8cee942d" "answer-95fe6bc0-80b2-59ce-8e98-8b6fb022689d" "answer-d22f515d-3390-5083-865d-1cfdc6e38f51" "answer-dc0f5c3c-5409-5295-8b20-7a4804f5c5b8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-00d2f4f8-927e-5d9b-a303-a838ea7066a1" :answer/id #uuid "00d2f4f8-927e-5d9b-a303-a838ea7066a1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-270d63ee-8d9e-556e-a5bb-984b8cee942d" :answer/id #uuid "270d63ee-8d9e-556e-a5bb-984b8cee942d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-95fe6bc0-80b2-59ce-8e98-8b6fb022689d" :answer/id #uuid "95fe6bc0-80b2-59ce-8e98-8b6fb022689d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5}\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d22f515d-3390-5083-865d-1cfdc6e38f51" :answer/id #uuid "d22f515d-3390-5083-865d-1cfdc6e38f51" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dc0f5c3c-5409-5295-8b20-7a4804f5c5b8" :answer/id #uuid "dc0f5c3c-5409-5295-8b20-7a4804f5c5b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-40959c8e-9382-5950-9324-5f121903c27d" :question/id #uuid "40959c8e-9382-5950-9324-5f121903c27d" :question/math-academy-id "q-113047" :question/problem "$23{\\text{i}}^{-1}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, using the laws of exponents, we can write\n\n$$\n23{\\text{i}}^{-1}=\\frac{23}{\\text{i}}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the numerator and denominator by $\\text{i},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{23}{\\text{i}}=\\frac{23}{\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{i}}{\\text{i}}=\\frac{23\\text{i}}{{\\text{i}}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now recall that ${\\text{i}}^{2}=-1.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{23\\text{i}}{{\\text{i}}^{2}}=\\frac{23\\text{i}}{(-1)}=\\frac{23}{(-1)}\\cdot \\text{i}=-23\\text{i}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c889ac42-82ad-583c-ac4c-14efe04c8381"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c889ac42-82ad-583c-ac4c-14efe04c8381" :answer-field/id #uuid "c889ac42-82ad-583c-ac4c-14efe04c8381" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-30a5e83d-857c-5c56-89fe-2c514067a79f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-30a5e83d-857c-5c56-89fe-2c514067a79f" "answer-c3b1eb34-fe49-528f-962a-0345cb5de9f3" "answer-8e95a151-896e-51ec-998e-4c2100f34265" "answer-b3292bda-9b83-5e17-b5db-c3daf4056235" "answer-542c8b6c-14b3-50ce-a50e-cdcc99c9e23e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-30a5e83d-857c-5c56-89fe-2c514067a79f" :answer/id #uuid "30a5e83d-857c-5c56-89fe-2c514067a79f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-23\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c3b1eb34-fe49-528f-962a-0345cb5de9f3" :answer/id #uuid "c3b1eb34-fe49-528f-962a-0345cb5de9f3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8e95a151-896e-51ec-998e-4c2100f34265" :answer/id #uuid "8e95a151-896e-51ec-998e-4c2100f34265" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b3292bda-9b83-5e17-b5db-c3daf4056235" :answer/id #uuid "b3292bda-9b83-5e17-b5db-c3daf4056235" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "23" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-542c8b6c-14b3-50ce-a50e-cdcc99c9e23e" :answer/id #uuid "542c8b6c-14b3-50ce-a50e-cdcc99c9e23e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "23\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-397ae4dc-5dce-54bd-9646-1b3867960198" :question/id #uuid "397ae4dc-5dce-54bd-9646-1b3867960198" :question/math-academy-id "q-66487" :question/problem "$8{\\text{i}}^{-1}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, using the laws of exponents, we can write\n\n$$\n8{\\text{i}}^{-1}=\\frac{8}{\\text{i}}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the numerator and denominator by $\\text{i},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8}{\\text{i}}=\\frac{8}{\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{i}}{\\text{i}}=\\frac{8\\text{i}}{{\\text{i}}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now recall that ${\\text{i}}^{2}=-1.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{8\\text{i}}{{\\text{i}}^{2}}=\\frac{8\\text{i}}{(-1)}=\\frac{8}{(-1)}\\cdot \\text{i}=-8\\text{i}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b3ebdfd7-1487-5255-822c-f756d3dffe5f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b3ebdfd7-1487-5255-822c-f756d3dffe5f" :answer-field/id #uuid "b3ebdfd7-1487-5255-822c-f756d3dffe5f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e49e1ad2-02e4-5a64-b217-e343adb1441e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4962bdcd-8c48-52ef-a215-673b0cd6e85a" "answer-e49e1ad2-02e4-5a64-b217-e343adb1441e" "answer-227e3695-f1f7-5799-8a85-616d2730eb59" "answer-46cb35cd-d4fd-54a6-9bec-45341e758acc" "answer-39dc5097-774b-5eb9-86c6-bbbc78406ee3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4962bdcd-8c48-52ef-a215-673b0cd6e85a" :answer/id #uuid "4962bdcd-8c48-52ef-a215-673b0cd6e85a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e49e1ad2-02e4-5a64-b217-e343adb1441e" :answer/id #uuid "e49e1ad2-02e4-5a64-b217-e343adb1441e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-227e3695-f1f7-5799-8a85-616d2730eb59" :answer/id #uuid "227e3695-f1f7-5799-8a85-616d2730eb59" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{8}\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-46cb35cd-d4fd-54a6-9bec-45341e758acc" :answer/id #uuid "46cb35cd-d4fd-54a6-9bec-45341e758acc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-39dc5097-774b-5eb9-86c6-bbbc78406ee3" :answer/id #uuid "39dc5097-774b-5eb9-86c6-bbbc78406ee3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186055966 :tutorial/content "Let's compute the first few powers of $\\textrm{i},$ where $\\textrm{i} = \\sqrt{-1}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{i}}^{0} & =1 \\\\ {\\text{i}}^{1} & =\\text{i} \\\\ {\\text{i}}^{2} & =-1 \\\\ {\\text{i}}^{3} & ={\\text{i}}^{2}\\cdot \\text{i}=(-1)\\cdot \\text{i}=-\\text{i} \\\\ {\\text{i}}^{4} & ={\\text{i}}^{2}\\cdot {\\text{i}}^{2}=(-1)\\cdot (-1)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can use these results to evaluate expressions containing powers of $\\textrm{i}.$ Let's take a look at some examples." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186055965 :tutorial/content "Let's remind ourselves of the first few powers of $\\textrm{i}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{i}}^{1} & =\\text{i} \\\\ {\\text{i}}^{2} & =-1 \\\\ {\\text{i}}^{3} & =-\\text{i} \\\\ {\\text{i}}^{4} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the fourth power, we return to the value of $1,$ which can also be written as $\\textrm{i}^0 = 1.$ This means that if we continue to increase the powers, we would cycle through the same four values once again, as shown below.\n\n![](images/5e/5e3f3a42dd591daf109e474eec99e446706e0d8e46f1252540839cd50d957463.png)\n\nSo, for $\\textrm{i}^5$ through $\\textrm{i}^8,$ the exact same pattern repeats. Remembering that $\\textrm{i}^4 = 1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\textrm{i}^5&=\\textrm{i}^4 \\cdot \\textrm{i} &= \\textrm{i}\\[5pt]\n\t\t\\textrm{i}^6&=\\textrm{i}^4 \\cdot \\textrm{i}^2 &=-1\\[5pt]\n\t\t\\textrm{i}^7&=\\textrm{i}^4 \\cdot \\textrm{i}^3 &= -\\textrm{i} \\[5pt]\n\t\t\\textrm{i}^8&=\\textrm{i}^4 \\cdot \\textrm{i}^4 &= 1 .\n\t}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, for $\\textrm{i}^9$ through to $\\textrm{i}^{12},$ the pattern repeats again:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\textrm{i}^9&=(\\textrm{i}^4)^2 \\cdot \\textrm{i} &= \\textrm{i}\\[5pt]\n\t\t\\textrm{i}^{10}&=(\\textrm{i}^4)^2 \\cdot \\textrm{i}^2 &=-1\\[5pt]\n\t\t\\textrm{i}^{11}&=(\\textrm{i}^4)^2 \\cdot \\textrm{i}^3 &= -\\textrm{i} \\[5pt]\n\t\t\\textrm{i}^{12}&=(\\textrm{i}^4)^2 \\cdot \\textrm{i}^4 &= 1 \n\t}\n$$\n\nTherefore, to simplify a higher integer power of $\\textrm{i},$ we *divide the power by $4$ and raise $\\textrm{i}$ to the remainder*.\n\nLet's see this idea in action." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054894 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166934 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-95759fde-a83b-52c8-a112-ac2f3137ea76" "question-c20fd0ed-71f4-5fd0-a6bc-687a270c962b"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-95759fde-a83b-52c8-a112-ac2f3137ea76" :question/id #uuid "95759fde-a83b-52c8-a112-ac2f3137ea76" :question/math-academy-id "q-332776" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t)-4 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{3s-4}{s(s-2)},\\,$\n${X}_{2}(s)=$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{2{x}_{1}(t)-4\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=2L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-4L\\{1\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-3=2{X}_{1}(s)-\\frac{4}{s} \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-0={X}_{1}(s)+{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\},$ and we have used the fact that $L\\{1\\}=\\frac{1}{s}.$\n\nNow, solving the first equation for ${X}_{1}(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-3 & =2{X}_{1}(s)-\\frac{4}{s} \\\\ (s-2){X}_{1}(s) & =3-\\frac{4}{s} \\\\ (s-2){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{3s-4}{s} \\\\ {X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{3s-4}{s(s-2)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the second equation and solving for ${X}_{2}(s),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{2}(s) & ={X}_{1}(s)+{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s-1){X}_{2}(s) & ={X}_{1}(s) \\\\ (s-1){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{3s-4}{s(s-2)} \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{3s-4}{s(s-1)(s-2)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the new system  in terms of parameter $s$ is \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{3s-4}{s(s-2)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{3s-4}{s(s-1)(s-2)}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-dbc222a5-fba5-54b1-8499-8bdfb1e8616c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-dbc222a5-fba5-54b1-8499-8bdfb1e8616c" :answer-field/id #uuid "dbc222a5-fba5-54b1-8499-8bdfb1e8616c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-7e75c2a5-efac-57be-8e90-38a4d983daed" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7e75c2a5-efac-57be-8e90-38a4d983daed"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7e75c2a5-efac-57be-8e90-38a4d983daed" :answer/id #uuid "7e75c2a5-efac-57be-8e90-38a4d983daed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3s-4}{s(s-2)(s-1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-c20fd0ed-71f4-5fd0-a6bc-687a270c962b" :question/id #uuid "c20fd0ed-71f4-5fd0-a6bc-687a270c962b" :question/math-academy-id "q-333060" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=4{x}_{1}(t)-3 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{2s-3}{s(s-4)}$ ,$\\,$\n${X}_{2}(s)=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{4{x}_{1}(t)-3\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=4L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-3L\\{1\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=-L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+2L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-2=4{X}_{1}(s)-\\frac{3}{s} \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)+1=-{X}_{1}(s)+2{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\},$ and we have used the fact that $L\\{1\\}=\\frac{1}{s}.$\n\nNow, solving the first equation for ${X}_{1}(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-2 & =4{X}_{1}(s)-\\frac{3}{s} \\\\ (s-4){X}_{1}(s) & =2-\\frac{3}{s} \\\\ (s-4){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{2s-3}{s} \\\\ {X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{2s-3}{s(s-4)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the second equation and solving for ${X}_{2}(s),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{2}(s)+1 & =-{X}_{1}(s)+2{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s-2){X}_{2}(s) & =-{X}_{1}(s)-1 \\\\ (s-2){X}_{2}(s) & =-(\\frac{2s-3}{s(s-4)})-1 \\\\ (s-2){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{-(2s-3)-s(s-4)}{s(s-4)} \\\\ (s-2){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{-2s+3-{s}^{2}+4s}{s(s-4)} \\\\ (s-2){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{-{s}^{2}+2s+3}{s(s-4)} \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{-{s}^{2}+2s+3}{s(s-2)(s-4)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the new system in terms of parameter $s$ is \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{2s-3}{s(s-4)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{-{s}^{2}+2s+3}{s(s-2)(s-4)}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-029ce416-5248-5a5e-a914-f27e3f878e0b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-029ce416-5248-5a5e-a914-f27e3f878e0b" :answer-field/id #uuid "029ce416-5248-5a5e-a914-f27e3f878e0b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-53cfc804-f2be-5e9c-8d5c-d7bbbd137c44" :answer-field/choices ["answer-53cfc804-f2be-5e9c-8d5c-d7bbbd137c44"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-53cfc804-f2be-5e9c-8d5c-d7bbbd137c44" :answer/id #uuid "53cfc804-f2be-5e9c-8d5c-d7bbbd137c44" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{-{s}^{2}+2s+3}{s(s-2)(s-4)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166935 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-78ae591d-ba8b-5d77-97cc-75f76d82b6a0"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-78ae591d-ba8b-5d77-97cc-75f76d82b6a0" :question/id #uuid "78ae591d-ba8b-5d77-97cc-75f76d82b6a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-333128" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t)+4 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t)-5,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}=\\frac{1}{s-2}-\\frac{2}{s},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}=-\\frac{2}{s-2}+\\frac{1}{s-3}+\\frac{3}{s}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{1}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-2}-\\frac{2}{s}\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-2}\\}-2\\,{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\} \\\\  & ={e}^{2\\cdot t}-2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={e}^{2t}-2 \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{2}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{-\\frac{2}{s-2}+\\frac{1}{s-3}+\\frac{3}{s}\\} \\\\  & =-2\\,{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-2}\\}+{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-3}\\}+3\\,{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\} \\\\  & =-2{e}^{2\\cdot t}+{e}^{3\\cdot t}+3\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={e}^{3t}-2{e}^{2t}+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t}-2 \\\\ {e}^{3t}-2{e}^{2t}+3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0560274e-eedd-5cd3-a9f0-b7e672a7b4b9" "answer-field-49de807c-da2e-59f0-b447-3aed1873fc9c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0560274e-eedd-5cd3-a9f0-b7e672a7b4b9" :answer-field/id #uuid "0560274e-eedd-5cd3-a9f0-b7e672a7b4b9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-81d22d6e-0616-586f-b9f3-42b8d530fd5f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-81d22d6e-0616-586f-b9f3-42b8d530fd5f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-81d22d6e-0616-586f-b9f3-42b8d530fd5f" :answer/id #uuid "81d22d6e-0616-586f-b9f3-42b8d530fd5f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e^{2t}-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-49de807c-da2e-59f0-b447-3aed1873fc9c" :answer-field/id #uuid "49de807c-da2e-59f0-b447-3aed1873fc9c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-9f2f8e1b-7ba5-5978-8caf-e60c554b76cb" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9f2f8e1b-7ba5-5978-8caf-e60c554b76cb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9f2f8e1b-7ba5-5978-8caf-e60c554b76cb" :answer/id #uuid "9f2f8e1b-7ba5-5978-8caf-e60c554b76cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2e^{2t}+e^{3t}+3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-f434441f-b9c7-5ee6-aaa1-b1b2afd5d471" :activity/id #uuid "f434441f-b9c7-5ee6-aaa1-b1b2afd5d471" :activity/title "Solving Inhomogeneous Systems of ODEs Using Laplace Transforms" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049381 :activity/course 17592186046644 :activity/steps ["step-b1745bc0-7e7d-5cce-a4e0-1fadf2d21096" "step-0d621a8f-cd0d-51e8-81b6-9ebdb390477f" "step-cd1c018d-a850-5621-b116-c5c0cc1a8c99" "step-c1ab16a5-ba62-5d1f-b985-9e65b24b08aa" "step-590ff66c-34e8-5381-aeda-9ccba67a75bc"] :activity/first-step "step-b1745bc0-7e7d-5cce-a4e0-1fadf2d21096" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-b1745bc0-7e7d-5cce-a4e0-1fadf2d21096" :step/id #uuid "b1745bc0-7e7d-5cce-a4e0-1fadf2d21096" :step/content "question-95759fde-a83b-52c8-a112-ac2f3137ea76" :step/next "step-0d621a8f-cd0d-51e8-81b6-9ebdb390477f" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-0d621a8f-cd0d-51e8-81b6-9ebdb390477f" :step/id #uuid "0d621a8f-cd0d-51e8-81b6-9ebdb390477f" :step/content "question-c20fd0ed-71f4-5fd0-a6bc-687a270c962b" :step/next "step-cd1c018d-a850-5621-b116-c5c0cc1a8c99" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-cd1c018d-a850-5621-b116-c5c0cc1a8c99" :step/id #uuid "cd1c018d-a850-5621-b116-c5c0cc1a8c99" :step/content "question-78ae591d-ba8b-5d77-97cc-75f76d82b6a0" :step/next "step-c1ab16a5-ba62-5d1f-b985-9e65b24b08aa" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-c1ab16a5-ba62-5d1f-b985-9e65b24b08aa" :step/id #uuid "c1ab16a5-ba62-5d1f-b985-9e65b24b08aa" :step/content 17592186308390 :step/next "step-590ff66c-34e8-5381-aeda-9ccba67a75bc" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-590ff66c-34e8-5381-aeda-9ccba67a75bc" :step/id #uuid "590ff66c-34e8-5381-aeda-9ccba67a75bc" :step/content 17592186308393 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054736 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-d1878d53-723f-5989-b8bc-003976423212" "question-c3ed3524-1800-5472-a34a-a2b28ed462d4"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-d1878d53-723f-5989-b8bc-003976423212" :question/id #uuid "d1878d53-723f-5989-b8bc-003976423212" :question/math-academy-id "q-70258" :question/problem "What is the magnitude of the number $z=-13\\text{i}?$" :question/worked-solution "The imaginary number $-13\\text{i}$ is equivalent to the complex number $z=0-13\\text{i}.$\n\nWe know that for a complex number $z=a+b\\text{i},$ the magnitude of $z$ is given by\n\n$$\n|z|=\\sqrt{{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nSo, the magnitude of $z=0-13\\text{i}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|z| & =\\sqrt{{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(0)^{2}+(-13)^{2}} \\\\  & =13.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-fea1f402-87f7-543c-a08b-8028f822c3a1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fea1f402-87f7-543c-a08b-8028f822c3a1" :answer-field/id #uuid "fea1f402-87f7-543c-a08b-8028f822c3a1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9313ceb2-8065-5a51-8891-b63edaff61bb" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4240242c-ccfc-5919-bcd1-23f365cf0d9c" "answer-5fc877af-90aa-504b-aeaa-80f58a1269ab" "answer-9313ceb2-8065-5a51-8891-b63edaff61bb" "answer-e910e0d2-e229-5e15-aa4e-2cbc5871b5be" "answer-81fce244-4b65-5986-bf17-3c08a29adf62"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4240242c-ccfc-5919-bcd1-23f365cf0d9c" :answer/id #uuid "4240242c-ccfc-5919-bcd1-23f365cf0d9c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-13" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5fc877af-90aa-504b-aeaa-80f58a1269ab" :answer/id #uuid "5fc877af-90aa-504b-aeaa-80f58a1269ab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\sqrt{13}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9313ceb2-8065-5a51-8891-b63edaff61bb" :answer/id #uuid "9313ceb2-8065-5a51-8891-b63edaff61bb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "13" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e910e0d2-e229-5e15-aa4e-2cbc5871b5be" :answer/id #uuid "e910e0d2-e229-5e15-aa4e-2cbc5871b5be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{-13}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-81fce244-4b65-5986-bf17-3c08a29adf62" :answer/id #uuid "81fce244-4b65-5986-bf17-3c08a29adf62" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{13}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054737 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-08d92dcc-49dd-5acf-9195-6229900ba610"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-08d92dcc-49dd-5acf-9195-6229900ba610" :question/id #uuid "08d92dcc-49dd-5acf-9195-6229900ba610" :question/math-academy-id "q-79466" :question/problem "Find $|z|$ if $z=2x+4c\\text{i},$ where $x$ and $c$ are real numbers." :question/worked-solution "For a complex number $z=a+b\\text{i},$ the magnitude of $z$ is given by\n\n$$\n|z|=\\sqrt{{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nFor the complex number $z=2x+4c\\text{i},$ we have $a=2x$ and $b=4c.$ So, the magnitude is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}|2x+4c\\text{i}| & =\\sqrt{(2x)^{2}+(4c)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}+16{c}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-17b8dedc-9dc9-5851-973e-6ace85b1c419"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-17b8dedc-9dc9-5851-973e-6ace85b1c419" :answer-field/id #uuid "17b8dedc-9dc9-5851-973e-6ace85b1c419" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7989544f-7ea6-5b3b-8e3c-3231d82c6955" :answer-field/choices ["answer-336f253c-9736-520b-8fb7-d41987f37473" "answer-8b810d0d-88c0-5a8f-aeca-ac3055abcc67" "answer-d4f229fc-d9e2-5832-9150-33c974b452ba" "answer-7989544f-7ea6-5b3b-8e3c-3231d82c6955" "answer-58e24837-7d55-5cdf-a839-e3afda08636c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-336f253c-9736-520b-8fb7-d41987f37473" :answer/id #uuid "336f253c-9736-520b-8fb7-d41987f37473" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{x}^{2}+4{c}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8b810d0d-88c0-5a8f-aeca-ac3055abcc67" :answer/id #uuid "8b810d0d-88c0-5a8f-aeca-ac3055abcc67" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2{x}^{2}+4{c}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d4f229fc-d9e2-5832-9150-33c974b452ba" :answer/id #uuid "d4f229fc-d9e2-5832-9150-33c974b452ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2{x}^{2}-4{c}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7989544f-7ea6-5b3b-8e3c-3231d82c6955" :answer/id #uuid "7989544f-7ea6-5b3b-8e3c-3231d82c6955" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}+16{c}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-58e24837-7d55-5cdf-a839-e3afda08636c" :answer/id #uuid "58e24837-7d55-5cdf-a839-e3afda08636c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}-16{c}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-c3ed3524-1800-5472-a34a-a2b28ed462d4" :question/id #uuid "c3ed3524-1800-5472-a34a-a2b28ed462d4" :question/math-academy-id "q-160277" :question/problem "What is the magnitude of the number $z=2\\text{i}?$" :question/worked-solution "The imaginary number $2\\text{i}$ is equivalent to the complex number $z=0+2\\text{i}.$\n\nWe know that for a complex number $z=a+b\\text{i},$ the magnitude of $z$ is given by\n\n$$\n|z|=\\sqrt{{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nSo, the magnitude of $z=0+2\\text{i}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|z| & =\\sqrt{{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(0)^{2}+(2)^{2}} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-35aa10d9-d0b5-5bf2-a319-9f587b8c0a83"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-35aa10d9-d0b5-5bf2-a319-9f587b8c0a83" :answer-field/id #uuid "35aa10d9-d0b5-5bf2-a319-9f587b8c0a83" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ab0f6764-317d-5061-9f80-de4f98c14068" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ab0f6764-317d-5061-9f80-de4f98c14068" "answer-008a9322-bc09-5270-b395-42f5ae02f992" "answer-eb76ce3d-4469-58f1-ae4b-06566734b7f8" "answer-2370feff-0720-50c4-8b43-d0d1aab5431b" "answer-8ef6c697-69ee-5d21-b15c-a353586495fa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ab0f6764-317d-5061-9f80-de4f98c14068" :answer/id #uuid "ab0f6764-317d-5061-9f80-de4f98c14068" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-008a9322-bc09-5270-b395-42f5ae02f992" :answer/id #uuid "008a9322-bc09-5270-b395-42f5ae02f992" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eb76ce3d-4469-58f1-ae4b-06566734b7f8" :answer/id #uuid "eb76ce3d-4469-58f1-ae4b-06566734b7f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2370feff-0720-50c4-8b43-d0d1aab5431b" :answer/id #uuid "2370feff-0720-50c4-8b43-d0d1aab5431b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8ef6c697-69ee-5d21-b15c-a353586495fa" :answer/id #uuid "8ef6c697-69ee-5d21-b15c-a353586495fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-f464d2cc-f0ba-5134-8a71-a42676f27b5c" :activity/id #uuid "f464d2cc-f0ba-5134-8a71-a42676f27b5c" :activity/title "The Magnitude of a Complex Number" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049831 :activity/course 17592186046647 :activity/steps ["step-7220f931-8523-5f49-b4d1-5a8977c89c7b" "step-a5133add-db8f-51c9-ba6d-cd7cde437126" "step-a94f0ad1-2aea-563c-ab9b-921184c576f7"] :activity/first-step "step-7220f931-8523-5f49-b4d1-5a8977c89c7b" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-7220f931-8523-5f49-b4d1-5a8977c89c7b" :step/id #uuid "7220f931-8523-5f49-b4d1-5a8977c89c7b" :step/content "question-d1878d53-723f-5989-b8bc-003976423212" :step/next "step-a5133add-db8f-51c9-ba6d-cd7cde437126" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-a5133add-db8f-51c9-ba6d-cd7cde437126" :step/id #uuid "a5133add-db8f-51c9-ba6d-cd7cde437126" :step/content "question-08d92dcc-49dd-5acf-9195-6229900ba610" :step/next "step-a94f0ad1-2aea-563c-ab9b-921184c576f7" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-a94f0ad1-2aea-563c-ab9b-921184c576f7" :step/id #uuid "a94f0ad1-2aea-563c-ab9b-921184c576f7" :step/content "question-c3ed3524-1800-5472-a34a-a2b28ed462d4" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186385351 :answer-field/choices 17592186385352] [:db/retract 17592186385351 :answer-field/choices 17592186385353] [:db/retract 17592186385351 :answer-field/choices 17592186385354] [:db/retract 17592186385351 :answer-field/choices 17592186385355] [:db/retract 17592186385351 :answer-field/choices 17592186385356] [:db/retract 17592186124976 :question/answer-fields 17592186122456] {:db/id 17592186124438 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ae3534f1-44d3-55be-bcdb-7634e16c97c5"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124976 :question/worked-solution "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $y=1.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $P(1,1,0)$ will be given by the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂x}{|}_{(1,1)}.$\n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂x}$ at $(1,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂z}{∂x}{|}_{(1,1)} & =3(1)+6(1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1\\cdot 1) \\\\  & =3+6\\operatorname{ln}⁡1 \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the point-slope form of a straight line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-z{|}_{(1,1)} & =\\frac{∂z}{∂x}{|}_{(1,1)}(x-1) \\\\ z-0 & =3(x-1) \\\\ z & =3x-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the curve $C$ at $P(1,1,0)$ can be given as the intersection of two planes, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}y=1 \\\\ z=3x-3\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186385351 :answer-field/correct "answer-940c73e1-fac8-5d96-a4d7-4f31a5f433a8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1cd26c8b-fb1c-5766-9fbe-ab3b0f2403f4" "answer-9ab403d6-b2c8-5db7-ac14-47e28ec612f9" "answer-940c73e1-fac8-5d96-a4d7-4f31a5f433a8" "answer-3cbc826e-b561-565f-a693-c12cb77c5362" "answer-d540c582-ba40-5073-81c9-81443650b392"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1cd26c8b-fb1c-5766-9fbe-ab3b0f2403f4" :answer/id #uuid "1cd26c8b-fb1c-5766-9fbe-ab3b0f2403f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=1 \\\\ z=2-2x\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9ab403d6-b2c8-5db7-ac14-47e28ec612f9" :answer/id #uuid "9ab403d6-b2c8-5db7-ac14-47e28ec612f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=1 \\\\ z=2x-2\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-940c73e1-fac8-5d96-a4d7-4f31a5f433a8" :answer/id #uuid "940c73e1-fac8-5d96-a4d7-4f31a5f433a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=1 \\\\ z=3x-3\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3cbc826e-b561-565f-a693-c12cb77c5362" :answer/id #uuid "3cbc826e-b561-565f-a693-c12cb77c5362" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=1 \\\\ z=3x\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d540c582-ba40-5073-81c9-81443650b392" :answer/id #uuid "d540c582-ba40-5073-81c9-81443650b392" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=1, \\\\ z=4x-4\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-ae3534f1-44d3-55be-bcdb-7634e16c97c5" :question/id #uuid "ae3534f1-44d3-55be-bcdb-7634e16c97c5" :question/math-academy-id "q-132594" :question/problem "The curve $C$ is the intersection of a surface $S,$ defined by $z=f(x,y),$ with the plane $y=\\pi .$ Given that the point $P(\\frac{1}{2},\\pi ,1)$ lies on $C$, and that ${f}_{x}=2x{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)$, find the equations of the tangent line to $C$ at $P.$" :question/worked-solution "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $y=\\pi .$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $P(\\frac{1}{2},\\pi ,1)$ will be given by the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂x}{|}_{(1/2,\\pi )}.$\n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂x}$ at $(\\frac{1}{2},\\pi ):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂z}{∂x}{|}_{(1/2,\\pi )} & =2(\\frac{1}{2}){e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi /2)}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & ={e}^{0}+1 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the point-slope form of a straight line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-z{|}_{(1/2,\\pi )} & =\\frac{∂z}{∂x}{|}_{(1/2,\\pi )}(x-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\ z-1 & =2(x-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\ z & =2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the curve $C$ at $P(\\frac{1}{2},\\pi ,1)$ can be given as the intersection of two planes, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}y=\\pi  \\\\ z=2x\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-37d670d1-3bff-5409-be4d-e79488473006"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-37d670d1-3bff-5409-be4d-e79488473006" :answer-field/id #uuid "37d670d1-3bff-5409-be4d-e79488473006" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ef0b5a29-3a47-5678-8b2a-9278853cd35b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-becf689a-2251-5072-95a8-008d1c2e4200" "answer-ef0b5a29-3a47-5678-8b2a-9278853cd35b" "answer-10528982-819d-558d-b7b9-c606e71872b0" "answer-7d86ddc1-2c7d-548c-9b05-047b8457b098" "answer-a8e89105-6501-5255-9bbc-617aef43299e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-becf689a-2251-5072-95a8-008d1c2e4200" :answer/id #uuid "becf689a-2251-5072-95a8-008d1c2e4200" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=\\pi  \\\\ z=2x+\\pi \\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ef0b5a29-3a47-5678-8b2a-9278853cd35b" :answer/id #uuid "ef0b5a29-3a47-5678-8b2a-9278853cd35b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=\\pi  \\\\ z=2x\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-10528982-819d-558d-b7b9-c606e71872b0" :answer/id #uuid "10528982-819d-558d-b7b9-c606e71872b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=\\pi  \\\\ z=3x+1\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7d86ddc1-2c7d-548c-9b05-047b8457b098" :answer/id #uuid "7d86ddc1-2c7d-548c-9b05-047b8457b098" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=\\pi  \\\\ z=x-1\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a8e89105-6501-5255-9bbc-617aef43299e" :answer/id #uuid "a8e89105-6501-5255-9bbc-617aef43299e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=\\pi  \\\\ z=x-\\pi \\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186268892 :question/worked-solution "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface with the plane $x=-2.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve $C$ at the point $P$ will be given by the partial derivative ${f}_{y}(-2,2).$ \n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative ${f}_{y}(x,y)$ at $(-2,2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(-2,2) & =(-2)^{2}(2)+2(-2)-(2) \\\\  & =8-4-2 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we use the point-slope form of a straight line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-f(-2,2) & ={f}_{y}(-2,2)(y-2) \\\\ z-3 & =2(y-2) \\\\ z & =2y-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the tangent line to the curve $C$ at $P(-2,2,3)$ can be given as the intersection of two planes:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=-2 \\\\ z=2y-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $x=-2,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨1,0,0⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $z=2y-1$ (or $2y-z-1=0$), a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨0,2,-1⟩.$\n\nFinally, to find a direction vector for the tangent line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨1,0,0⟩\\times ⟨0,2,-1⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =j+2\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a tangent vector to $C$ at $P$ is $j+2\\,k.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "activity-dee62c26-4f96-5315-9736-66f2027d8581" :activity/id #uuid "dee62c26-4f96-5315-9736-66f2027d8581" :activity/title "Geometric Interpretations of Partial Derivatives" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186050158 :activity/course 17592186046658 :activity/steps ["step-39707566-6312-542f-af0b-85f44247ceeb" "step-f46d0be1-bd90-5c9e-ab3f-e22acfe2493d" "step-b5bc4d9f-ec45-5df0-ba2f-64b35987a453" "step-1430ce69-365b-5d69-8d4b-3d05c2d08e10" "step-a34f7fed-6748-57b7-896d-3a0ab90523d6"] :activity/first-step "step-39707566-6312-542f-af0b-85f44247ceeb" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-39707566-6312-542f-af0b-85f44247ceeb" :step/id #uuid "39707566-6312-542f-af0b-85f44247ceeb" :step/content 17592186124976 :step/next "step-f46d0be1-bd90-5c9e-ab3f-e22acfe2493d" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-f46d0be1-bd90-5c9e-ab3f-e22acfe2493d" :step/id #uuid 