fy this ratio by dividing both numbers in a ratio by $2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,2 &  & : & \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,4 &  \\\\ \\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,2 &  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,2 &  \\\\ \\,\\,1 &  & : &  & \\,\\,\\,2 & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of pentagons to the total shapes is $1:2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5b42a0ed-8cc4-538a-846f-4d271e746063"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5b42a0ed-8cc4-538a-846f-4d271e746063" :answer-field/id #uuid "5b42a0ed-8cc4-538a-846f-4d271e746063" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-fc699391-fd04-52df-b409-e770247a3ce6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ff467776-5b6b-511a-ad55-110c0788fd36" "answer-fc699391-fd04-52df-b409-e770247a3ce6" "answer-f68f1bd9-0968-5373-95e0-ba9f203e08c4" "answer-fcfa165d-4b9d-54cb-812e-73d65dba9b12" "answer-d0003dfa-a1b9-55b2-9d01-caf97c1db2c7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ff467776-5b6b-511a-ad55-110c0788fd36" :answer/id #uuid "ff467776-5b6b-511a-ad55-110c0788fd36" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1:1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fc699391-fd04-52df-b409-e770247a3ce6" :answer/id #uuid "fc699391-fd04-52df-b409-e770247a3ce6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1:2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f68f1bd9-0968-5373-95e0-ba9f203e08c4" :answer/id #uuid "f68f1bd9-0968-5373-95e0-ba9f203e08c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1:3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fcfa165d-4b9d-54cb-812e-73d65dba9b12" :answer/id #uuid "fcfa165d-4b9d-54cb-812e-73d65dba9b12" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2:3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d0003dfa-a1b9-55b2-9d01-caf97c1db2c7" :answer/id #uuid "d0003dfa-a1b9-55b2-9d01-caf97c1db2c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3:2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186147544 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8134e1ae-9578-5877-ab86-0666cefb2b4c"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-8134e1ae-9578-5877-ab86-0666cefb2b4c" :question/id #uuid "8134e1ae-9578-5877-ab86-0666cefb2b4c" :question/math-academy-id "q-350261" :question/problem "Maya and Priya are café owners. In the previous season, $55%$ of Maya’s orders were takeout, while the decimal proportion of Priya’s orders that were takeout was $0.8.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. Less than half of Maya's orders were takeout.\n\nII. More than half of Priya's orders were takeout.\n\nIII. Maya had a greater percentage of takeout orders compared to Priya." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed, since \n\n$$\n55%>50%,\n$$\n\nmore than half of Maya's orders were takeout.\n\n- Statement II is true. Notice that \n\n$$\n0.8>0.5.\n$$\n\nSo, more than half of Priya's orders were takeout.\n\n- Statement III is false. We can compare $55%$ and $0.8$ by converting the decimal into a percent. \n\nTo do this, we multiply it by $100:$\n\n$$\n0.8\\times 100=80%\n$$\n\nSince  $55%<80%,$ Maya did not have a greater percentage of takeout orders compared to Priya.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-90a3f767-62b1-56e7-8914-d9fc2589ce88"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-90a3f767-62b1-56e7-8914-d9fc2589ce88" :answer-field/id #uuid "90a3f767-62b1-56e7-8914-d9fc2589ce88" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b59f6c09-9eee-5a65-a69f-2fd0dc79df4a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-aef19ca5-ff9c-50d9-8e0b-543cb86c89db" "answer-85d382c2-60ee-52a0-8af7-005ba470406e" "answer-13d60628-2e34-5a04-8810-5657a4599223" "answer-b59f6c09-9eee-5a65-a69f-2fd0dc79df4a" "answer-c463c709-bb2f-50b7-94ad-28fe7da2872a"] :db/ensure [:answer-fie