" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-c2eabaac-f3d6-5e89-863c-f6a16abf0577" :step/id #uuid "c2eabaac-f3d6-5e89-863c-f6a16abf0577" :step/content "question-e4257f22-304f-5aae-a7d4-d381f535406f" :step/next "step-a49f6873-757d-575d-8ab4-bef4cddedb52" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-a49f6873-757d-575d-8ab4-bef4cddedb52" :step/id #uuid "a49f6873-757d-575d-8ab4-bef4cddedb52" :step/content "question-b2e2b3d0-06c7-5374-8f2a-5e2b0c04b187" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073740 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e345f1f6-4e4b-57f5-a961-226088f10a38" "question-2295df98-ce45-53e5-ab4e-ebfbd4881c7a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186074373 :question/problem "![](images/38/3865ec425991f0d8ceae82f002d0096f2fd2ea56743173e754b15472b7c85031.png)\n\nWhat number is missing from the boxes in the statement below?\n\nThe ratio of triangles to hexagons is $1:\\boxed{}\\,$ because there is $1$ triangle for every $\\boxed{}$ hexagon." :question/worked-solution "First, we count the number of triangles. We see that there are $3$ triangles.\n\nThen, we count the number of hexagons. We see that there are $3$ hexagons.\n\nSo the ratio of triangles to hexagons is $3:3.$\n\nWe can simplify this ratio by dividing both numbers by $3$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,3 &  & : & \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,3 &  \\\\ \\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,3 &  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,3 &  \\\\ \\,\\,1 &  & : &  & \\,\\,\\,1 & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that $1:1$ is equivalent to $3:3.$ \n\nSo, the complete statement is\n\"The ratio of triangles to hexagons is $1:1$ because there is $1$ triangle for every $1$ hexagon.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186072476 :answer-field/correct 17592186072479 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-e345f1f6-4e4b-57f5-a961-226088f10a38" :question/id #uuid "e345f1f6-4e4b-57f5-a961-226088f10a38" :question/math-academy-id "q-92799" :question/problem "Dominick has $8$ steel marbles and $14$ glass marbles. What number is missing from the boxes in the statement below?\n\nThe ratio of steel marbles to glass marbles is $4:\\boxed{}\\,$ because there are $4$ steel marbles for every $\\boxed{}\\,$ glass marbles." :question/worked-solution "Since there are $8$ steel marbles and $14$ glass marbles, the ratio of steel marbles to glass marbles is $8:14.$\n\nWe can simplify this ratio by dividing both numbers by $2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,8 &  & : & \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,14 &  \\\\ \\,\\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,2 &  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,2 &  \\\\ \\,\\,\\,4 &  & : &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,7 & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThat means that $4:7$ is equivalent to $8:14.$ \n\nSo, the complete statement is\n\"The ratio of steel marbles to glass marbles is $4:7$ because there are $4$ steel marbles for every $7$ glass marbles.\"\n\nHence, the missing number is $7.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-25ccbefd-df3d-54b1-82ef-3bcd139c5460"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-25ccbefd-df3d-54b1-82ef-3bcd139c5460" :answer-field/id #uuid "25ccbefd-df3d-54b1-82ef-3bcd139c5460" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a24fea6b-a341-5cf3-808c-27c825cb1528" :answer-field/choices ["answer-58839e93-46a7-5cba-a7a8-b5b186148928" "answer-f8464049-28bd-5b10-888e-adf0b228fb7d" "answer-1034259d-6a50-53d2-8b2a-548dd4a01b24" "answer-a24fea6b-a341-5cf3-808c-27c825cb1528" "answer-9818025a-7109-5370-82e1-53582885ae81"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-58839e93-46a7-5cba-a7a8-b5b186148928" :answer/id #uuid "58839e93-46a7-5cba-a7a8-b5b186148928" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f8464049-28bd-5b10-888e-adf0b228fb7d" :answer/id #uuid "f8464049-28bd-5b10-888e-adf0b228fb7d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1034259d-6a50-53d2-8b2a-548dd4a01b24" :answer/id #uuid "1034259d-6a50-53d2-8b2a-548dd4a01b24" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a24fea6b-a341-5cf3-808c-27c825cb1528" :answer/id #uuid "a24fea6b-a341-5cf3-808c-27c825cb1528" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9818025a-7109-5370-82e1-53582885ae81" :answer/id #uuid "9818025a-7109-5370-82e1-53582885ae81" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-2295df98-ce45-53e5-ab4e-ebfbd4881c7a" :question/id #uuid "2295df98-ce45-53e5-ab4e-ebfbd4881c7a" :question/math-academy-id "q-131918" :question/problem "If there are $21$ pears and $15$ apples, then what number is missing from the boxes in the statement below?\n\nThe ratio of pears to apples is $7:\\boxed{}\\,$ because there are $7$ pears for every $\\boxed{}\\,$ apples." :question/worked-solution "Since there are $21$ pears and $15$ apples, the ratio of pears to apples is $21:15.$\n\nWe can simplify this ratio by dividing both numbers by $3:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,21 &  & : & \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,15 &  \\\\ \\,\\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,3 &  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,3 &  \\\\ \\,\\,\\,7 &  & : &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,5 & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThat means that $21:15$ is equivalent to $7:5.$ \n\nSo, the complete statement is \"The ratio of pears to apples is $7:5\\,$ because there are $7$ pears for every $5\\,$ apples.\"\n\nTherefore, the missing number is $5.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c4ada293-0707-5fcb-af41-5176ed9ea4fa"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c4ada293-0707-5fcb-af41-5176ed9ea4fa" :answer-field/id #uuid "c4ada293-0707-5fcb-af41-5176ed9ea4fa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-39f0e787-bfeb-525d-962e-fbc0be1dea03" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f2cded69-fda